WEBVTT

1
00:00:59.392 --> 00:01:01.272
Gentlemen!

2
00:01:01.392 --> 00:01:04.992
That's it for today.
Turn everything off!

3
00:01:05.112 --> 00:01:08.192
Change your clothes.
The buses are waiting.

4
00:01:08.312 --> 00:01:12.752
Get a move on!
Are you deaf? I said turn it off.

5
00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:18.192
Hurry up! The factory's closing
while we wait for raw materials.

6
00:01:18.312 --> 00:01:20.392
You will be paid.

7
00:01:20.632 --> 00:01:25.552
We'll contact you next week
about your wages.

8
00:01:25.672 --> 00:01:28.672
Go back to the dorms!

9
00:01:28.792 --> 00:01:34.712
Get out of your uniforms,
take all your things and get on the buses.

10
00:01:34.832 --> 00:01:37.592
If you dawdle,
you won't find a ride out tonight.

11
00:01:46.592 --> 00:01:49.592
We're closing! Get up, hurry!

12
00:01:49.912 --> 00:01:51.392
Move it!

13
00:01:51.752 --> 00:01:55.512
And don't even think about going to HR.

14
00:01:55.632 --> 00:01:57.872
Don't cause trouble for yourselves.

15
00:01:57.992 --> 00:02:00.552
The factory could press charges against you.

16
00:02:00.672 --> 00:02:03.032
You could be arrested

17
00:02:03.152 --> 00:02:05.392
and lose your pay.

18
00:03:32.232 --> 00:03:33.552
Hello.

19
00:03:35.232 --> 00:03:36.552
Have a seat.

20
00:04:07.592 --> 00:04:10.672
Hello, Bayram.
Thank you.

21
00:04:10.792 --> 00:04:14.792
- Sit down, please.
- No, thank you.

22
00:04:16.232 --> 00:04:17.952
- Excuse me.
- It's okay.

23
00:05:59.072 --> 00:06:00.792
"Eight months no pay
28 months no healthcare"

24
00:06:57.952 --> 00:06:59.272
Hello.

25
00:07:04.552 --> 00:07:09.792
Ghardashali, I'm not imposing
anything on anyone.

26
00:07:10.112 --> 00:07:13.392
Personally, I'm still mourning.

27
00:07:14.992 --> 00:07:17.432
You're free to do what you think is right.

28
00:07:17.552 --> 00:07:21.072
Bayram, you know that
as long as you're in mourning,

29
00:07:21.192 --> 00:07:22.992
we'll all wear black.

30
00:07:29.112 --> 00:07:32.392
Say a prayer for the deceased!

31
00:07:38.192 --> 00:07:40.352
May Gholam rest in peace,
my dear Bayram.

32
00:07:40.472 --> 00:07:41.872
May God protect you.

33
00:07:41.992 --> 00:07:44.272
- A small gift.
- You shouldn't have.

34
00:07:44.392 --> 00:07:48.592
Gholam was my cousin,
but he was like a father to me.

35
00:07:48.712 --> 00:07:51.592
That's very kind, really,
but you shouldn't have.

36
00:07:51.712 --> 00:07:55.792
If I may, I'd also like to trim
your hair and beard

37
00:07:55.952 --> 00:07:57.792
to take you out of mourning.

38
00:07:58.152 --> 00:08:00.192
Are you suddenly a barber?

39
00:08:00.752 --> 00:08:03.032
Go sit down and let us convince him.

40
00:08:03.152 --> 00:08:05.472
- This way.
- Come sit.

41
00:08:05.592 --> 00:08:06.912
Come have a seat.

42
00:08:08.032 --> 00:08:10.992
- Sit.
- Make yourself comfortable.

43
00:08:11.192 --> 00:08:16.192
Bayram, as long as you wear black
the family will, too.

44
00:08:16.592 --> 00:08:20.592
Alright, trim your hair and beards
and stop wearing black.

45
00:08:20.952 --> 00:08:22.592
With all due respect,

46
00:08:23.232 --> 00:08:25.192
Gholam was our patriarch,

47
00:08:25.312 --> 00:08:28.232
we're waiting for you to name his successor.

48
00:08:28.352 --> 00:08:29.792
But I'm still mourning.

49
00:08:29.912 --> 00:08:33.232
- It's been a year!
- Succession obeys its own rules.

50
00:08:33.352 --> 00:08:36.472
- You'll read his will when I see fit.
- His will?

51
00:08:36.592 --> 00:08:40.192
- You haven't opened it yet?
- Of course I have.

52
00:08:40.392 --> 00:08:41.952
And no one knows anything?

53
00:08:42.072 --> 00:08:45.352
- My father asked for one year deferment.
- And now?

54
00:08:45.472 --> 00:08:47.072
I'm not ready yet.

55
00:08:47.192 --> 00:08:52.912
Dad, four couples are waiting
to plan their weddings.

56
00:08:53.032 --> 00:08:55.592
You're not speaking for yourself?

57
00:08:55.712 --> 00:08:59.592
Everyone's saying it.
Come here, Dad.

58
00:09:00.392 --> 00:09:03.192
I understand him. He's tired of waiting.

59
00:09:03.312 --> 00:09:08.192
We all thought your son
would get married after the 40th day,

60
00:09:08.312 --> 00:09:11.392
and that the others would follow.

61
00:09:12.672 --> 00:09:16.912
Honestly, if you let these poor kids
get on with their lives,

62
00:09:17.032 --> 00:09:19.792
no one will think less of you.

63
00:09:27.312 --> 00:09:29.072
Please, Bayram.

64
00:09:29.192 --> 00:09:31.192
Let us say a prayer!

65
00:10:38.832 --> 00:10:42.992
The bastards are the ones who flee,
counting on their colleagues

66
00:10:43.112 --> 00:10:44.792
to fight for their wages.

67
00:10:50.512 --> 00:10:52.392
Just use the trimmer.

68
00:10:53.312 --> 00:10:54.632
I'll let you know.

69
00:10:55.032 --> 00:10:56.352
I'll call you back.

70
00:10:57.072 --> 00:10:58.392
Bye.

71
00:11:02.392 --> 00:11:05.392
Name the successor today
and get it over with.

72
00:11:05.512 --> 00:11:09.952
- Are you pressing for Ghardashali?
- He offered to plan your son's wedding.

73
00:11:10.072 --> 00:11:13.032
- My son has a father.
- Excuse me, Bayram.

74
00:11:13.152 --> 00:11:18.432
Ghardashali deserves to be patriarch.
But I'm the eldest.

75
00:11:18.552 --> 00:11:21.752
Say, Ghardashali? Is he the eldest?

76
00:11:21.872 --> 00:11:23.272
- Who?
- Esmail.

77
00:11:23.392 --> 00:11:26.592
That piker shirks weddings
to avoid giving gifts.

78
00:11:26.712 --> 00:11:30.472
- He's after free lunches.
- That's no way to speak in public.

79
00:11:30.592 --> 00:11:33.312
He hasn't even helped his own children.

80
00:11:33.432 --> 00:11:34.992
What a patriarch he'd make!

81
00:11:35.672 --> 00:11:38.432
Show some decency.
Who's older, you or him?

82
00:11:38.552 --> 00:11:41.272
- Me, obviously.
- God is my witness,

83
00:11:41.392 --> 00:11:44.832
I don't expect to be Gholam's successor.

84
00:11:44.952 --> 00:11:47.952
Be my guest. We're all behind you!

85
00:11:48.072 --> 00:11:50.952
I was six when you were born, Ghardashali.

86
00:11:51.072 --> 00:11:52.632
My mother nursed you.

87
00:11:52.752 --> 00:11:57.192
- It's not only about age.
- Exactly.

88
00:11:57.312 --> 00:11:59.432
I was just saying I'm the eldest.

89
00:11:59.552 --> 00:12:03.872
While Ghardashali was Gholam's friend
in his last moments.

90
00:12:03.992 --> 00:12:05.472
Well said!

91
00:12:05.592 --> 00:12:09.992
If Gholam is satisfied,
we'll all be satisfied!

92
00:15:04.912 --> 00:15:07.232
Did you know it was my crib?

93
00:15:07.352 --> 00:15:08.792
It was mine.

94
00:15:09.072 --> 00:15:11.112
Yes, it was all of ours.

95
00:15:11.232 --> 00:15:14.832
- You still in there, Dad?
- "I can't help it. It hurts."

96
00:15:14.952 --> 00:15:17.392
Leila, you've used up all the city's water.

97
00:15:17.552 --> 00:15:19.592
"Take me to see a doctor, Alireza."

98
00:15:20.072 --> 00:15:23.392
- Take him where?
- Ignore him, he's fine.

99
00:15:27.392 --> 00:15:29.552
Where's my car key? Dad!

100
00:15:29.672 --> 00:15:31.272
"You didn't pay me yesterday."

101
00:15:31.392 --> 00:15:34.912
I was at the garage all day.
Where's the second key?

102
00:15:35.032 --> 00:15:37.192
"If you touch it,"

103
00:15:37.312 --> 00:15:40.592
"I'll call the police on you!"

104
00:15:41.712 --> 00:15:46.992
Do what you did to Parviz.
Go ahead and take me to court.

105
00:15:52.392 --> 00:15:54.792
Shut the water off, I don't have any!

106
00:15:56.312 --> 00:15:59.832
- Let's take the elevator.
- I can't breathe in that thing!

107
00:15:59.952 --> 00:16:02.632
- Is it a boy?
- I swear it is.

108
00:16:02.752 --> 00:16:04.992
You swear nonsense.

109
00:16:05.472 --> 00:16:08.992
- Swear on Manouchehr's life!
- On Farhad's life, it's a boy.

110
00:16:09.672 --> 00:16:11.512
That means it's a girl.

111
00:16:11.632 --> 00:16:13.912
Don't bug them about naming him Gholam.

112
00:16:14.032 --> 00:16:17.472
- Butt out.
- You're the one who's butting in.

113
00:16:17.592 --> 00:16:19.632
For Gholam's memorial,

114
00:16:19.752 --> 00:16:23.672
I was the first to be dressed in white
and have my beard trimmed.

115
00:16:23.792 --> 00:16:25.672
It's expected of me.

116
00:16:25.792 --> 00:16:28.632
- Come meet the baby, will you?
- Where's Manouchehr?

117
00:16:28.752 --> 00:16:31.792
The sissy can't handle the smell of hospitals.

118
00:16:36.632 --> 00:16:41.232
- Finally, someone who's not empty-handed!
- Hello, my sweethearts!

119
00:16:41.352 --> 00:16:42.672
Good to see you.

120
00:16:43.032 --> 00:16:48.192
- You're lucky this one's a boy.
- Yep. He'd keep harassing me otherwise.

121
00:16:50.472 --> 00:16:51.792
Congratulations.

122
00:16:52.392 --> 00:16:57.192
- Let me kiss my grandchild.
- You can't kiss a newborn's face.

123
00:16:57.312 --> 00:17:00.152
- It's not a boy.
- 'Course it is, check.

124
00:17:00.272 --> 00:17:03.392
- Have her undress him then.
- He'll catch cold.

125
00:17:03.632 --> 00:17:07.392
For every one of those five girls,
they told me it was a boy.

126
00:17:07.672 --> 00:17:12.112
After 2 years, I'd suddenly see them
wearing skirts and earrings.

127
00:17:12.232 --> 00:17:14.072
This time, they won't fool me.

128
00:17:14.192 --> 00:17:17.632
- Undress him!
- It's not easy to unwrap.

129
00:17:17.752 --> 00:17:20.352
Don't delude me, evil woman!

130
00:17:20.472 --> 00:17:23.912
Calm down, sir.
You're in a hospital. Please leave.

131
00:17:24.032 --> 00:17:26.232
Forgive him.
You're embarrassing us.

132
00:17:26.352 --> 00:17:29.392
Leila, show him
before he has a heart attack.

133
00:17:29.552 --> 00:17:30.872
Come look.

134
00:17:32.912 --> 00:17:34.232
Hold on.

135
00:17:36.312 --> 00:17:39.392
There we are.

136
00:17:46.592 --> 00:17:48.192
What a joy.

137
00:17:49.512 --> 00:17:50.992
It's a boy!

138
00:17:53.912 --> 00:17:56.592
- It's a boy.
- See that?

139
00:17:56.712 --> 00:17:59.112
Didn't he have enough boys?

140
00:17:59.232 --> 00:18:01.792
He's your humble servant.

141
00:18:08.472 --> 00:18:11.592
Look at those lashes.
He's so handsome...

142
00:18:37.272 --> 00:18:39.992
Don't pout, eat.
I'll take you to a doctor tomorrow.

143
00:18:54.032 --> 00:18:56.512
Damn that Brock Lesnar!

144
00:18:56.632 --> 00:19:00.352
The only guy who can beat Undertaker
is Lesnar.

145
00:19:00.472 --> 00:19:02.792
- It's all phony.
- It is not.

146
00:19:02.912 --> 00:19:06.112
Hardy jumps from a 30-ft ladder
onto Big Show's face.

147
00:19:06.352 --> 00:19:07.752
Is that phony?

148
00:19:07.872 --> 00:19:12.472
She forgets our names,
but she knows the wrestlers' by heart!

149
00:19:12.592 --> 00:19:16.872
- That's your fault.
- Orton's gonna crush Lesnar, Mom.

150
00:19:16.992 --> 00:19:20.712
- He's no Shawn Michaels.
- I have the same build as Orton, don't I?

151
00:19:20.832 --> 00:19:24.872
Stop it, you orangutan!
Put your clothes back on!

152
00:19:24.992 --> 00:19:26.392
Are they dressed?

153
00:19:26.512 --> 00:19:29.712
Sister-in-law, it's my back again.
Take the baby.

154
00:19:29.832 --> 00:19:32.472
- I'm so sorry.
- Ouch!

155
00:19:32.592 --> 00:19:34.792
Don't do the dishes.

156
00:19:35.192 --> 00:19:37.832
Get married and that pain will go away.

157
00:19:37.952 --> 00:19:41.272
Farhad, you can't just eat and do nothing.

158
00:19:41.392 --> 00:19:43.472
We should deal with the dishes.

159
00:19:43.632 --> 00:19:45.992
- I'm still eating.
- I mean in general.

160
00:19:46.112 --> 00:19:48.552
You ruminate like a cow. That's enough.

161
00:19:48.672 --> 00:19:51.832
- Do you mean me or Parviz?
- Wait till we clear the dishes.

162
00:19:51.952 --> 00:19:54.352
In two minutes, he'll have his pants down.

163
00:19:54.472 --> 00:19:58.992
- Dad, blow for the baby.
- He's in a hurry to go home.

164
00:19:59.592 --> 00:20:01.792
Because he knows what he's done.

165
00:20:02.032 --> 00:20:03.352
Congratulations.

166
00:20:03.632 --> 00:20:05.392
What's the matter with you?

167
00:20:05.552 --> 00:20:07.992
May he have a long and happy life.

168
00:20:09.472 --> 00:20:13.072
Tell me, what's the name
on the birth certificate?

169
00:20:13.192 --> 00:20:14.792
The name you asked for.

170
00:20:15.312 --> 00:20:17.792
- What name is that?
- Gholam.

171
00:20:17.952 --> 00:20:19.272
Gholam.

172
00:20:19.632 --> 00:20:22.192
- Show me his record.
- We don't have it.

173
00:20:22.632 --> 00:20:23.952
What is this then?

174
00:20:24.072 --> 00:20:26.712
I picked it up today. Parviz didn't know.

175
00:20:26.832 --> 00:20:28.792
Read it and tell me what they named the kid.

176
00:20:31.912 --> 00:20:34.192
- It's Gholam.
- Gholam.

177
00:20:34.592 --> 00:20:36.392
What is it to us?

178
00:20:37.592 --> 00:20:40.192
Alireza, are they telling me the truth?

179
00:20:50.952 --> 00:20:52.992
- Yes. It's Gholam.
- Where does it say Gholam?

180
00:20:53.112 --> 00:20:55.792
Point the word out to me.

181
00:20:56.952 --> 00:20:58.272
Right here.

182
00:21:05.352 --> 00:21:06.832
Give me my bank card.

183
00:21:06.952 --> 00:21:09.592
- Why?
- I don't want you to have it.

184
00:21:32.992 --> 00:21:34.312
"Death Announcement"

185
00:21:39.952 --> 00:21:41.272
"Gholam"

186
00:21:41.992 --> 00:21:43.312
"Pouyan"

187
00:21:50.072 --> 00:21:51.392
It's not Gholam!

188
00:21:51.512 --> 00:21:54.112
Get out, you dirty liars!

189
00:21:54.232 --> 00:21:57.312
I knew the bastards wouldn't listen.

190
00:21:57.432 --> 00:22:00.072
Get out, you thief!

191
00:22:00.192 --> 00:22:02.992
- Think of your heart.
- You're scaring the girls.

192
00:22:03.112 --> 00:22:05.752
- Get lost, all of you.
- They're gone.

193
00:22:05.872 --> 00:22:08.472
- You, come here.
- What's gotten into you, Dad?

194
00:22:08.592 --> 00:22:10.912
Have you lost your mind?

195
00:22:11.032 --> 00:22:13.632
He steals my pension
and he steals from my home.

196
00:22:13.752 --> 00:22:15.992
Leila put it in my bag.

197
00:22:16.992 --> 00:22:19.192
Raheleh is breastfeeding, Dad!

198
00:22:23.152 --> 00:22:26.872
After a year, my wife finally
comes to dinner. Thank you.

199
00:22:26.992 --> 00:22:28.312
Get over here.

200
00:22:47.192 --> 00:22:48.912
Stop it, Dad.

201
00:22:52.432 --> 00:22:55.192
He doesn't want to name his son Gholam!

202
00:22:55.472 --> 00:22:56.832
Go to hell, both of you!

203
00:22:56.952 --> 00:22:59.872
You could've named
one of your four sons Gholam!

204
00:22:59.992 --> 00:23:03.072
Gholam was still alive then.
It isn't done, fool.

205
00:23:03.192 --> 00:23:05.152
Screw your traditions!

206
00:23:05.272 --> 00:23:07.752
Bayram can name his own grandkid Gholam.

207
00:23:07.872 --> 00:23:09.192
We'd pre-empt him!

208
00:23:09.312 --> 00:23:12.832
- What for?
- To hold our heads up high.

209
00:23:12.952 --> 00:23:16.272
Did being named after your father
bring me luck?

210
00:23:16.392 --> 00:23:20.992
Why would I have to name my son
after your half-wit cousin?

211
00:23:49.232 --> 00:23:52.352
You're eligible for unemployment benefits.

212
00:23:52.472 --> 00:23:55.312
Stay home every day
from 8 a.m. to 2 p.m.

213
00:23:55.432 --> 00:23:57.512
We run inspections.

214
00:23:57.632 --> 00:24:01.712
If you're absent,
your benefits will be suspended.

215
00:24:01.832 --> 00:24:03.952
Excuse me, miss, I filled this out.

216
00:24:04.072 --> 00:24:05.392
Sign here.

217
00:24:05.752 --> 00:24:07.392
First floor, employment department.

218
00:24:08.512 --> 00:24:10.192
When do I look for a job?

219
00:24:10.312 --> 00:24:15.792
There are a lot of layoffs these days.
We're very strict.

220
00:24:16.152 --> 00:24:18.112
To keep your benefits,

221
00:24:18.232 --> 00:24:20.712
- follow the rules listed here.
- Thanks.

222
00:24:20.832 --> 00:24:22.792
Miss, this letter came for me.

223
00:24:24.152 --> 00:24:26.392
- Booth number 7, income department.
- Thank you.

224
00:24:28.232 --> 00:24:29.792
There's a seat here.

225
00:24:30.632 --> 00:24:32.992
I'll go get a number.

226
00:24:33.112 --> 00:24:34.432
Have a seat, Dad.

227
00:24:40.672 --> 00:24:42.512
- Wait in line.
- It's just a form.

228
00:24:42.632 --> 00:24:44.592
Internal medicine, Jourablou.

229
00:24:48.072 --> 00:24:49.392
It's packed...

230
00:24:49.512 --> 00:24:52.592
It's a state hospital. Could be worse.

231
00:24:54.432 --> 00:24:55.752
Excuse me, ma'am.

232
00:25:00.832 --> 00:25:02.792
Dad, we're right here.

233
00:25:14.672 --> 00:25:18.552
Could you please not ask Mom and Dad
how they're feeling?

234
00:25:18.672 --> 00:25:21.032
- Why?
- I've worked hard weening them off

235
00:25:21.152 --> 00:25:22.672
asking for a doctor every day.

236
00:25:22.792 --> 00:25:24.552
You show up, and here we go again.

237
00:25:24.672 --> 00:25:26.232
So they're afraid of you?

238
00:25:26.352 --> 00:25:28.992
Worse, they hate me.

239
00:25:29.152 --> 00:25:30.792
But they're sick...

240
00:25:31.952 --> 00:25:33.992
You have no idea, Alireza.

241
00:25:34.352 --> 00:25:36.872
At their age, they need check-ups.

242
00:25:36.992 --> 00:25:40.192
Every doctor in town knows us.

243
00:25:40.312 --> 00:25:43.392
I'm only here for four days.

244
00:25:44.632 --> 00:25:46.192
Why are you saying that?

245
00:25:48.032 --> 00:25:49.992
Things are tense, so you run for it?

246
00:25:50.112 --> 00:25:51.832
I have to go back to work.

247
00:25:51.952 --> 00:25:55.192
You can't lie to me
the way you lie to the others.

248
00:25:55.352 --> 00:25:58.432
You're out of a job, like your brothers.

249
00:25:58.552 --> 00:26:00.392
You're unemployed.

250
00:26:01.032 --> 00:26:05.592
You only have to spend one night at home
for me to know everything about you.

251
00:26:06.112 --> 00:26:10.632
- You were fired.
- You get fired when you do something wrong.

252
00:26:10.752 --> 00:26:12.872
The owner was crooked,
the factory went bankrupt.

253
00:26:12.992 --> 00:26:16.472
They laid us off. We weren't fired.

254
00:26:16.592 --> 00:26:19.592
Then stop pretending you're on vacation.

255
00:26:21.032 --> 00:26:24.392
Tell them you can't take them
to the doctor's every day

256
00:26:24.512 --> 00:26:28.592
because you have to be home
to not lose your benefits.

257
00:26:29.832 --> 00:26:31.152
Sit down.

258
00:26:39.712 --> 00:26:42.032
Who else knows I lost my job?

259
00:26:42.152 --> 00:26:46.952
Mom was thanking God she had a son
who'd have a pension.

260
00:26:47.072 --> 00:26:49.912
Since she found out, she's lost.

261
00:26:50.032 --> 00:26:52.792
- How did she find out?
- I told her.

262
00:26:52.912 --> 00:26:56.192
I'll find a job quickly.
I don't like being idle.

263
00:26:57.312 --> 00:27:00.792
A job won't change things.
We have to do something.

264
00:27:06.032 --> 00:27:07.352
Alireza...

265
00:27:08.552 --> 00:27:10.592
start a juicy business

266
00:27:11.112 --> 00:27:14.512
and involve your brothers
to help them out of poverty.

267
00:27:14.632 --> 00:27:18.672
Don't pressure me.
Why would that be my responsibility?

268
00:27:18.792 --> 00:27:21.672
I tried, but I couldn't pull it off.

269
00:27:21.792 --> 00:27:25.152
Why not ask Manouchehr?
You have three other brothers.

270
00:27:25.272 --> 00:27:27.992
Manouchehr is one of the things
I'm worried about!

271
00:27:28.592 --> 00:27:32.992
If we do nothing,
he'll get caught with all his scheming.

272
00:27:33.312 --> 00:27:37.152
I was counting on you to back me,
to take my side,

273
00:27:37.272 --> 00:27:39.592
and act with discernment.

274
00:27:40.592 --> 00:27:44.992
Parviz can't carry his weight.
He's always looking for a place to sit.

275
00:27:45.352 --> 00:27:48.592
- Farhad thinks with his abs.
- Pretend I never came.

276
00:27:48.712 --> 00:27:53.152
- I can't, you're here.
- My presence wouldn't change anything.

277
00:27:53.272 --> 00:27:57.472
My salary is what keeps us from starving.

278
00:27:57.592 --> 00:27:58.912
But...

279
00:28:01.232 --> 00:28:03.432
Sorry, can we swap seats?

280
00:28:03.552 --> 00:28:04.872
Yes.

281
00:28:05.272 --> 00:28:06.592
Thanks.

282
00:28:10.232 --> 00:28:12.232
What about my wages?

283
00:28:12.352 --> 00:28:16.312
Your income, mine
and dad's pension is still not enough.

284
00:28:16.432 --> 00:28:18.592
They've stagnated all their lives.

285
00:28:18.712 --> 00:28:20.392
Not "they," we!

286
00:28:21.192 --> 00:28:24.072
We're not stagnating, we're regressing.

287
00:28:24.192 --> 00:28:27.512
Regressing from where?
What did we have to lose?

288
00:28:27.632 --> 00:28:28.952
Our youth.

289
00:28:29.752 --> 00:28:31.192
Which is slipping away.

290
00:28:31.312 --> 00:28:34.192
Let's try to not end up old and beggarly.

291
00:28:34.312 --> 00:28:35.632
Brother...

292
00:28:35.992 --> 00:28:37.992
don't listen to Mom and Dad.

293
00:28:38.312 --> 00:28:40.072
By night, they sleep.

294
00:28:40.192 --> 00:28:43.592
By day, they think about sleeping soundly.

295
00:28:44.632 --> 00:28:48.152
Everyone's miserable at home.
They hate each other.

296
00:28:48.272 --> 00:28:53.792
It breaks my heart to see them
take their anger out on each other.

297
00:28:56.072 --> 00:28:58.192
Start a business with them.

298
00:29:03.232 --> 00:29:07.992
Even though I hate seeing my brothers jobless,
I was happy you were fired.

299
00:29:09.352 --> 00:29:11.792
I was finally going to be able to ask you

300
00:29:13.152 --> 00:29:15.392
not to abandon your brothers.

301
00:29:15.752 --> 00:29:17.592
They're on their own.

302
00:29:18.192 --> 00:29:22.792
They're lost and broke.
Don't leave them like this.

303
00:29:23.752 --> 00:29:27.792
If you leave again,
what will become of them?

304
00:29:30.672 --> 00:29:33.072
Tell them to get their act together.

305
00:29:33.192 --> 00:29:35.632
I have. They can't.

306
00:29:35.752 --> 00:29:39.152
- Why not?
- They don't know how to start a business.

307
00:29:39.272 --> 00:29:43.192
- And I do?
- If somebody does, it's you.

308
00:29:44.752 --> 00:29:47.752
Suppose we did. Who'd work?
Those lazy bums?

309
00:29:47.872 --> 00:29:50.032
They're not lazy. They're working.

310
00:29:50.152 --> 00:29:52.232
But they have meanly jobs.

311
00:29:52.352 --> 00:29:55.592
- Alright, but they're morons.
- They're not morons.

312
00:29:55.872 --> 00:29:59.272
Poverty makes you lose your confidence
and look stupid.

313
00:29:59.392 --> 00:30:02.192
I don't like conflict, sis'.

314
00:30:02.632 --> 00:30:04.992
It stresses me out when everyone yells.

315
00:30:05.112 --> 00:30:08.192
I want to work out of town
and come back on occasion.

316
00:30:08.352 --> 00:30:12.672
I'm begging you, don't involve me.

317
00:30:12.792 --> 00:30:14.672
They're your family.

318
00:30:14.792 --> 00:30:18.232
I gave up a year of back wages,

319
00:30:18.352 --> 00:30:21.392
to get away from the ruckus at the factory.

320
00:30:22.112 --> 00:30:24.872
I hate my family's hysteria.

321
00:30:24.992 --> 00:30:27.792
Insecure jobs make people hysterical.

322
00:30:27.912 --> 00:30:30.592
The harder you work, the poorer you are.

323
00:30:31.512 --> 00:30:34.792
Poverty is hard to shake off.

324
00:30:34.912 --> 00:30:37.832
The more you swallow, the more there is.

325
00:30:37.952 --> 00:30:40.592
All of that is why I left.

326
00:30:41.192 --> 00:30:46.592
So you're saying you came back
only to stay if things were rosy.

327
00:30:46.832 --> 00:30:48.152
And if they weren't...

328
00:30:51.152 --> 00:30:52.792
Don't cry, Leila.

329
00:30:54.432 --> 00:30:58.392
Can't you start something
that's actually a real job?

330
00:31:00.032 --> 00:31:02.952
So when you fill out a form,
under "occupation"

331
00:31:03.072 --> 00:31:04.992
you can put something down?

332
00:31:33.152 --> 00:31:36.032
Yes, I told him about it.

333
00:31:36.152 --> 00:31:37.472
It's settled.

334
00:31:38.912 --> 00:31:41.472
Why do you neglect yourself so much?

335
00:31:41.592 --> 00:31:43.552
You weren't this fat last time.

336
00:31:43.672 --> 00:31:46.592
I don't get much exercise
with this damn job.

337
00:31:46.952 --> 00:31:50.352
- He started drinking.
- Shut up. It's my thyroid.

338
00:31:50.472 --> 00:31:53.232
Doctor says drinking doesn't help the thyroid.

339
00:31:53.352 --> 00:31:55.592
Our place is small, the kids are noisy.

340
00:31:56.432 --> 00:31:59.192
Sometimes I drink to get to sleep.

341
00:31:59.312 --> 00:32:01.272
- Where you going?
- To the bathroom.

342
00:32:01.392 --> 00:32:03.952
- Let it dry.
- I really need to go.

343
00:32:04.072 --> 00:32:05.712
- Got any cash?
- Yes.

344
00:32:05.832 --> 00:32:07.152
Go ahead.

345
00:32:11.352 --> 00:32:13.792
White tiles need constant cleaning.

346
00:32:15.152 --> 00:32:17.152
Why'd you ask us to come?

347
00:32:17.272 --> 00:32:21.192
They want to turn the bathroom
into a bunch of shops.

348
00:32:21.512 --> 00:32:23.992
He's right. It's being green-lit.

349
00:32:24.152 --> 00:32:27.112
- What's it to us?
- I thought you should see it.

350
00:32:27.232 --> 00:32:29.672
Alireza, we have to act quickly.

351
00:32:29.792 --> 00:32:33.112
The other shop owners
will soon get their claws into it.

352
00:32:33.232 --> 00:32:35.912
To become wealthy,
you have to be in the know.

353
00:32:36.032 --> 00:32:37.752
Where'd you hear it?

354
00:32:37.872 --> 00:32:39.432
Nowhere. It's my flare.

355
00:32:39.552 --> 00:32:40.872
Stop it.

356
00:32:41.112 --> 00:32:44.392
I overheard your financial manager here.

357
00:32:44.792 --> 00:32:48.312
I asked if we could buy a small shop
with a loan.

358
00:32:48.432 --> 00:32:50.472
- Price per square foot?
- 15 to 20 million.

359
00:32:50.592 --> 00:32:51.992
We can't afford it.

360
00:32:52.112 --> 00:32:54.192
I can barely afford a square foot.

361
00:32:54.312 --> 00:32:56.232
The others are worse off.

362
00:32:56.352 --> 00:32:58.872
Give it a chance.
Maybe we can pull it off.

363
00:32:58.992 --> 00:33:00.312
My boss likes me.

364
00:33:00.472 --> 00:33:02.232
Even without a deposit, we can't.

365
00:33:02.352 --> 00:33:04.792
Are you a naysayer like Manouchehr now?

366
00:33:04.912 --> 00:33:07.992
Fine. Where would we find the money?

367
00:33:18.712 --> 00:33:21.112
Alright, never mind.

368
00:33:21.232 --> 00:33:23.152
You're not letting them think.

369
00:33:23.272 --> 00:33:25.552
Buying a shop requires money, not thought.

370
00:33:25.672 --> 00:33:27.792
This scale is off.

371
00:33:28.992 --> 00:33:30.312
If you want it, it'll work.

372
00:33:30.712 --> 00:33:32.032
Suppose I did.

373
00:33:32.632 --> 00:33:34.552
You have to actually want it!

374
00:33:34.672 --> 00:33:36.792
Is it all on me?

375
00:33:37.952 --> 00:33:40.392
I'm all for it. That's why I'm here.

376
00:33:40.832 --> 00:33:43.032
I asked you to come. I want it.

377
00:33:43.152 --> 00:33:44.792
If we're just talking, I do too.

378
00:33:44.912 --> 00:33:46.792
We all want it deep down.

379
00:33:47.712 --> 00:33:49.992
Same here. Me too.

380
00:33:51.912 --> 00:33:53.232
Where you going?

381
00:33:53.952 --> 00:33:56.552
Last time, I paid for two visits.

382
00:33:56.672 --> 00:33:58.112
I don't remember that.

383
00:33:58.232 --> 00:34:00.592
- How much?
- What did you do?

384
00:34:00.992 --> 00:34:03.512
What? I used the bathroom for a minute.

385
00:34:03.632 --> 00:34:07.192
You took longer than a minute. Gimme 500.

386
00:34:09.632 --> 00:34:13.672
- Do you have change this time?
- No. I won't charge you next time.

387
00:34:13.792 --> 00:34:17.592
- What if you forget again?
- You'll remind me, jog my memory.

388
00:34:20.032 --> 00:34:23.192
If he files a complaint,
I'll have no other job for you.

389
00:34:39.592 --> 00:34:42.472
Wake him up, so he can sleep in his bed.

390
00:34:42.592 --> 00:34:46.792
Since he got his pacemaker,
he often sleeps like that.

391
00:34:46.992 --> 00:34:50.552
He says that if he lies down,
he feels like he's dying.

392
00:34:50.672 --> 00:34:51.992
Go listen.

393
00:35:19.992 --> 00:35:21.312
Look, son.

394
00:35:21.552 --> 00:35:25.592
If I don't bandage myself,
it tingles all night.

395
00:35:25.792 --> 00:35:29.792
- Shouldn't we see a doctor?
- Sure. I'll see to it tomorrow.

396
00:35:30.072 --> 00:35:32.792
We have a lot to do tomorrow.
Don't make promises.

397
00:35:35.192 --> 00:35:36.792
Here, Mom, take your pills.

398
00:35:39.432 --> 00:35:42.552
And use your ointment against the tingling.

399
00:35:42.672 --> 00:35:45.952
- Dad.
- Don't, he just fell asleep.

400
00:35:46.072 --> 00:35:48.992
- Take your pills.
- He'll take them tomorrow.

401
00:35:49.112 --> 00:35:51.392
If he doesn't take them,
he'll be sick tomorrow.

402
00:35:59.512 --> 00:36:01.392
Mom loves the big guys.

403
00:36:01.632 --> 00:36:04.392
Triple H, Brock Lesnar, Big Show.

404
00:36:04.512 --> 00:36:06.992
That's why she loves Parviz so much.

405
00:36:07.232 --> 00:36:10.792
With her bandages,
she could all knock 'em all out.

406
00:36:14.272 --> 00:36:15.992
Don't get in front of the TV.

407
00:36:16.632 --> 00:36:20.352
I called Manouchehr about the shop.

408
00:36:20.472 --> 00:36:24.752
- And?
- He says that our problem is the deposit,

409
00:36:24.872 --> 00:36:27.072
but that he's got a plan.

410
00:36:27.192 --> 00:36:31.352
Is it seducing old, depressed, rich women?

411
00:36:31.472 --> 00:36:35.192
- "Sugar mommy!"
- He set up an appointment for tomorrow night.

412
00:36:35.472 --> 00:36:37.992
He'll explain everything.

413
00:36:38.952 --> 00:36:41.872
He was ashamed
to say we were his brothers.

414
00:36:41.992 --> 00:36:43.992
Why do business with us now?

415
00:36:54.632 --> 00:36:56.272
- Good evening.
- Good evening.

416
00:36:56.392 --> 00:36:57.912
- Good evening.
- Good evening.

417
00:36:58.032 --> 00:36:59.592
Why are you here?

418
00:37:00.072 --> 00:37:02.512
- Why shouldn't I be?
- Wait at my place.

419
00:37:02.632 --> 00:37:05.712
It's a man's thing, sis'.

420
00:37:05.832 --> 00:37:07.712
Then he can't come.

421
00:37:07.832 --> 00:37:10.592
Should I open my mouth to dump on you?

422
00:37:11.352 --> 00:37:13.592
He shits from his mouth?

423
00:37:14.232 --> 00:37:17.792
- That's disgusting!
- Just asking.

424
00:37:17.992 --> 00:37:20.792
Go upstairs and rest until we get back.

425
00:37:20.912 --> 00:37:23.072
I can't go up all those stairs.

426
00:37:23.192 --> 00:37:27.192
Take the elevator,
it's in perfect working order.

427
00:37:27.312 --> 00:37:30.392
I'd rather die than get in that thing.

428
00:37:30.992 --> 00:37:33.192
It takes Parviz up easy.

429
00:37:33.352 --> 00:37:36.592
- Nice.
- You weigh less. Here's the remote.

430
00:37:37.112 --> 00:37:39.872
Don't sign anything until we all discuss it.

431
00:37:39.992 --> 00:37:42.392
- Sure.
- We're late, hurry.

432
00:37:45.592 --> 00:37:46.912
How you doing, brother?

433
00:37:47.592 --> 00:37:49.192
Good, thanks.

434
00:38:39.752 --> 00:38:41.552
Don't drive off the cliff!

435
00:38:41.672 --> 00:38:46.832
Why on earth would anyone pay money
to buy an apartment in this shithole?

436
00:38:46.952 --> 00:38:50.512
Wait till I get the deed. You'll see.

437
00:38:50.632 --> 00:38:54.552
- You don't have a deed?
- Not until the gas is hooked up.

438
00:38:54.672 --> 00:38:56.512
Good God, there's no gas?

439
00:38:56.632 --> 00:39:00.312
His unit has two windowless
40 sq. ft bedrooms.

440
00:39:00.432 --> 00:39:03.072
He doesn't even have access to the staircase.

441
00:39:03.192 --> 00:39:05.992
- Is that true?
- He's full of shit.

442
00:39:06.112 --> 00:39:08.032
It used to be two stories, two owners.

443
00:39:08.152 --> 00:39:11.512
The downstairs guy
illegally built a basement.

444
00:39:11.632 --> 00:39:15.832
So the upstairs guy
built a revenge apartment on the roof.

445
00:39:15.952 --> 00:39:19.192
- And?
- The downstairs guy blocked off the staircase

446
00:39:19.312 --> 00:39:21.232
and we fitted an elevator outside.

447
00:39:21.352 --> 00:39:23.672
Who'd buy a place like that?

448
00:39:23.792 --> 00:39:27.032
You can brag about your brother
who lives uptown.

449
00:39:27.152 --> 00:39:29.912
Uptown ended way before this back alley.

450
00:39:30.032 --> 00:39:32.672
This is a shantytown, you moron.

451
00:39:32.792 --> 00:39:35.312
Blockhead saw it. I have a majestic view.

452
00:39:35.432 --> 00:39:39.632
Sure, majestic until someone
builds right in front of it.

453
00:39:39.752 --> 00:39:41.992
Or city hall tears it down.

454
00:39:42.952 --> 00:39:44.272
Look at those cars!

455
00:39:44.832 --> 00:39:46.392
Uptown, he says.

456
00:39:48.032 --> 00:39:49.592
You're something else, Manouchehr.

457
00:40:00.952 --> 00:40:04.792
Let's go. Prepare to be blown away.

458
00:41:07.152 --> 00:41:10.912
Thanks, Mahmoud. Great tea!

459
00:41:11.032 --> 00:41:12.352
Help yourself.

460
00:41:13.232 --> 00:41:15.192
I'll leave the tray here.

461
00:41:16.672 --> 00:41:20.232
Mahmoud has a super job here.

462
00:41:20.352 --> 00:41:24.592
You're welcome.
High income, low hassle.

463
00:41:24.832 --> 00:41:28.312
He's making this offer as a favor to me.

464
00:41:28.432 --> 00:41:32.792
No. Now that we're roommates,
I love him like a brother.

465
00:41:32.912 --> 00:41:36.312
- He lives at your place?
- No, I live at his.

466
00:41:36.432 --> 00:41:38.632
Six months ago, I was homeless.

467
00:41:38.752 --> 00:41:41.272
You set all this up in six months?

468
00:41:41.392 --> 00:41:44.392
I didn't set it up, but I run it now.

469
00:41:44.512 --> 00:41:46.792
Does it belong to you or not?

470
00:41:46.912 --> 00:41:49.112
It belongs to whoever works here.

471
00:41:49.232 --> 00:41:51.392
I'm sorry, what's the job exactly?

472
00:41:51.632 --> 00:41:53.992
- Let me explain...
- May I?

473
00:41:54.272 --> 00:41:58.312
This is a car leasing company.

474
00:41:58.432 --> 00:42:02.272
The factory delivers a Kia Pride
in thirty days for 23 million.

475
00:42:02.392 --> 00:42:06.632
Mahmoud delivers it in three months,
but for 20 million.

476
00:42:06.752 --> 00:42:08.192
Wait, Manouchehr.

477
00:42:08.312 --> 00:42:11.552
Do you get the cars from the factory
or a middleman?

478
00:42:11.672 --> 00:42:12.992
Neither.

479
00:42:13.152 --> 00:42:16.152
We never actually deliver the cars.

480
00:42:16.272 --> 00:42:21.272
I'm sorry,
you take people's money and disappear?

481
00:42:21.392 --> 00:42:23.392
- Come on, brother...
- It's okay.

482
00:42:23.672 --> 00:42:26.712
A fraudster leaves the cash
under his mattress.

483
00:42:26.832 --> 00:42:29.992
I have ten bank accounts.
Manouchehr knows this.

484
00:42:30.112 --> 00:42:33.352
You take the money
and never deliver the car. How?

485
00:42:33.472 --> 00:42:35.272
- What's his name?
- Alireza.

486
00:42:35.392 --> 00:42:36.992
Ali, it's not complicated.

487
00:42:37.112 --> 00:42:39.392
Listen and you'll understand.

488
00:42:39.552 --> 00:42:42.392
Before me, my brother-in-law was here.

489
00:42:42.512 --> 00:42:46.312
My brother-in-law presold 1,000 cars
and left with the money.

490
00:42:46.432 --> 00:42:48.192
I took over the office.

491
00:42:48.672 --> 00:42:53.632
First, I presold a 1,000 Prides
to pay off my brother-in-law's debt,

492
00:42:53.752 --> 00:42:57.152
to the same people,
before they filed a complaint.

493
00:42:57.272 --> 00:43:02.512
Then, I presold another 1,000 Prides
and pocketed the money.

494
00:43:02.632 --> 00:43:04.672
So if you take over this office:

495
00:43:04.792 --> 00:43:07.152
First you pay off my debt,

496
00:43:07.272 --> 00:43:11.232
then you pocket the money
from the next 1,000 presales.

497
00:43:11.352 --> 00:43:13.632
And pass the buck to the next guy.

498
00:43:13.752 --> 00:43:16.192
Who will do the same.

499
00:43:16.312 --> 00:43:19.792
First, pay off your debt.
Then, pocket the money.

500
00:43:19.912 --> 00:43:21.512
- So on and so forth.
- It's a cycle.

501
00:43:21.632 --> 00:43:26.272
I get it. I'm sorry,
so you're looking for a successor?

502
00:43:26.392 --> 00:43:28.272
For someone to take over the office.

503
00:43:28.392 --> 00:43:31.232
Mahmoud is looking for someone
to replace him.

504
00:43:31.352 --> 00:43:35.072
That's all you do from this huge office?

505
00:43:35.192 --> 00:43:38.792
Listen. 1,000 times 20 million
is 20 billion tomans.

506
00:43:38.912 --> 00:43:40.872
In current dollars...

507
00:43:40.992 --> 00:43:43.792
- What's the exchange rate? 5,000.
- 5,000.

508
00:43:44.112 --> 00:43:45.672
That's 4 million dollars.

509
00:43:45.792 --> 00:43:47.792
We'll be millionaires in dollars!

510
00:43:47.912 --> 00:43:50.272
Don't people file complaints?

511
00:43:50.392 --> 00:43:52.432
Not for two-month delays.

512
00:43:52.552 --> 00:43:54.152
Suppose a handful do.

513
00:43:54.272 --> 00:43:57.472
We buy a couple of Prides, end of story.

514
00:43:57.592 --> 00:43:59.032
Not necessary!

515
00:43:59.152 --> 00:44:01.792
Throw them back their 20, and they're happy.

516
00:44:02.592 --> 00:44:05.392
In my opinion, it's very low risk.

517
00:44:06.392 --> 00:44:07.712
Ali...

518
00:44:08.392 --> 00:44:11.472
I left my wife and kids
with 80 million in debt

519
00:44:11.592 --> 00:44:14.992
and came to Tehran
to sit on that couch.

520
00:44:15.672 --> 00:44:19.792
When they pitched it to me,
I was apprehensive.

521
00:44:20.312 --> 00:44:22.912
But now,
my house back home is so big

522
00:44:23.032 --> 00:44:26.992
my wife calls the cops
to find the kids.

523
00:44:29.832 --> 00:44:32.352
My three offices are proof it works.

524
00:44:32.472 --> 00:44:35.392
But you're living in my brother's hovel?

525
00:44:35.512 --> 00:44:37.392
Question of opportunity.

526
00:44:37.712 --> 00:44:41.592
An uptown address,
cheaper than the south, is a no-brainer.

527
00:44:41.712 --> 00:44:44.992
I've seen Mahmoud's advancement
with my own two eyes.

528
00:44:45.352 --> 00:44:46.672
It's impressive.

529
00:44:46.792 --> 00:44:48.512
Are your permits in order?

530
00:44:48.632 --> 00:44:51.392
If they weren't, we couldn't advertise.

531
00:44:52.552 --> 00:44:55.792
How much would it cost for us to take over?

532
00:44:56.152 --> 00:44:59.992
The rent and advertising costs
are my gift for a year.

533
00:45:00.672 --> 00:45:03.992
But one of you has to sign,
accept responsibility.

534
00:45:04.112 --> 00:45:07.272
Seriously, what more could we ask for?

535
00:45:07.392 --> 00:45:10.392
- It's a golden opportunity.
- He has a point, Alireza.

536
00:45:12.192 --> 00:45:13.752
And what do we do?

537
00:45:13.872 --> 00:45:15.392
Legally speaking,

538
00:45:15.512 --> 00:45:18.632
if I put the company in my name,

539
00:45:18.752 --> 00:45:21.992
I need a board of directors
of at least four people.

540
00:45:22.232 --> 00:45:25.192
I would be the chairman.

541
00:45:25.472 --> 00:45:27.192
You the CEO.

542
00:45:27.352 --> 00:45:30.592
We thought Parviz
could be vice-chairman.

543
00:45:31.472 --> 00:45:33.232
- At your service.
- Thank you.

544
00:45:33.352 --> 00:45:37.192
And Farhad
could be an ordinary board member.

545
00:45:37.632 --> 00:45:39.272
That's what I had in mind.

546
00:45:39.392 --> 00:45:44.592
- Thanks to Mahmoud's advice, of course.
- My pleasure.

547
00:45:45.152 --> 00:45:46.472
One more!

548
00:45:46.912 --> 00:45:48.992
On the count of three, laugh.

549
00:45:49.112 --> 00:45:50.992
One, two, three, laugh!

550
00:45:54.112 --> 00:45:55.432
It's a keeper.

551
00:45:58.712 --> 00:46:00.032
Thanks.

552
00:46:05.592 --> 00:46:10.232
I'll say it again: Kick your roommate out.
If he goes down, you go down.

553
00:46:10.352 --> 00:46:12.792
As soon as I pay off my debt, I will.

554
00:46:12.912 --> 00:46:16.552
A mere glimpse of your schemes terrifies me.

555
00:46:16.672 --> 00:46:18.552
I should've gone alone.

556
00:46:18.672 --> 00:46:22.152
Had I known you would freak out
and contaminate the others,

557
00:46:22.272 --> 00:46:26.672
- I would've kept you out of it.
- Call a spade a spade. He's weak.

558
00:46:26.792 --> 00:46:29.992
Rejecting your scams
makes him weak and scared?

559
00:46:30.112 --> 00:46:33.312
In 8 years at the factory,
he hasn't taken 8 weeks off.

560
00:46:33.432 --> 00:46:36.592
If his ex hadn't married the neighbor,
he would've stayed.

561
00:46:36.712 --> 00:46:39.392
What's that got to do with anything?

562
00:46:40.032 --> 00:46:42.352
Save your breath, Leila.

563
00:46:42.472 --> 00:46:46.752
Instead of telling us what not to do,
tell us what to do.

564
00:46:46.872 --> 00:46:50.272
Do anything
except what Manouchehr suggests.

565
00:46:50.392 --> 00:46:52.912
Like the shop, for example.

566
00:46:53.032 --> 00:46:55.472
- There you go.
- With what money?

567
00:46:55.592 --> 00:46:58.032
Said like that, none of us will find any.

568
00:46:58.152 --> 00:47:01.952
- How should I say it?
- Do you only get excited if it's illegal?

569
00:47:02.072 --> 00:47:04.872
I'm hard enough on myself.
Get off my case.

570
00:47:04.992 --> 00:47:07.392
Don't listen to your moronic brother.

571
00:47:08.472 --> 00:47:09.912
Tell me how much you have.

572
00:47:10.032 --> 00:47:12.272
If it's to start a business,

573
00:47:12.392 --> 00:47:17.712
- I have about 20 million to contribute.
- Farhad, what about you?

574
00:47:17.832 --> 00:47:23.592
If I stop driving
and sell the car, 20 million.

575
00:47:23.712 --> 00:47:25.712
- Parviz?
- I swear I have nothing,

576
00:47:25.832 --> 00:47:27.592
except 5 million in debt.

577
00:47:27.712 --> 00:47:29.792
And the money I gave you last month?

578
00:47:30.112 --> 00:47:31.552
In front of everyone?

579
00:47:31.672 --> 00:47:37.352
- With that 4 million I paid off another debt.
- How about you, Leila?

580
00:47:37.472 --> 00:47:40.832
I have 8 million,
and half a gold coin from work.

581
00:47:40.952 --> 00:47:42.592
What about you, mastermind?

582
00:47:42.792 --> 00:47:44.112
800 million.

583
00:47:44.432 --> 00:47:46.392
Nothing, of course! Zilch.

584
00:47:46.752 --> 00:47:48.072
I don't want this.

585
00:47:49.392 --> 00:47:51.632
You want us to leave, is that it?

586
00:47:51.752 --> 00:47:54.992
He wants to have dinner
with his roommate.

587
00:47:55.192 --> 00:47:58.392
I can't eat at home
when I'm not in my house clothes.

588
00:47:58.512 --> 00:48:02.032
- How cute.
- Go change, instead of being a grump.

589
00:48:02.152 --> 00:48:04.152
For once you have us over.

590
00:48:04.272 --> 00:48:07.512
It's not foolish
to think you could sell your home.

591
00:48:07.632 --> 00:48:09.832
- I think it's foolish.
- Don't be offended.

592
00:48:09.952 --> 00:48:11.312
How much is it worth?

593
00:48:11.432 --> 00:48:15.832
Best case scenario, 120 million.
But there are a lot of obstacles.

594
00:48:15.952 --> 00:48:17.472
- What obstacles?
- Lots.

595
00:48:17.592 --> 00:48:19.552
- Like what?
- Like the deed.

596
00:48:19.672 --> 00:48:21.792
My roommate, my debt. Want more?

597
00:48:23.352 --> 00:48:24.672
It's a good time to buy.

598
00:48:24.792 --> 00:48:28.192
It's an investment
that will always retain its value.

599
00:48:28.312 --> 00:48:30.952
Prices keep shooting up.

600
00:48:31.072 --> 00:48:33.592
I examined all your crummy suggestions

601
00:48:33.712 --> 00:48:36.632
before settling on the deal
I offered you tonight.

602
00:48:36.752 --> 00:48:39.952
You did not.
You've been daydreaming.

603
00:48:40.072 --> 00:48:41.472
What're you driving at?

604
00:48:41.592 --> 00:48:43.872
Don't count on my apartment.

605
00:48:43.992 --> 00:48:47.192
What if we help you remove the obstacles?

606
00:48:48.552 --> 00:48:51.632
If you don't put this down
to me being stupid,

607
00:48:51.752 --> 00:48:56.152
I still harbor the tiny hope
of getting my wife back.

608
00:48:56.272 --> 00:48:59.792
- Then what would I do?
- We'd rent you another place.

609
00:49:00.952 --> 00:49:03.792
I'd rather live in a slum

610
00:49:03.912 --> 00:49:05.592
than be a tenant.

611
00:49:05.712 --> 00:49:09.272
Didn't you forge my passport
to go hang out in Thailand?

612
00:49:09.392 --> 00:49:11.232
You don't need your wife.

613
00:49:11.352 --> 00:49:14.072
He doesn't want to give it to us.
Leave him alone.

614
00:49:14.192 --> 00:49:16.712
Are you playing good guy again?

615
00:49:16.832 --> 00:49:19.792
We're a bunch of asses

616
00:49:19.912 --> 00:49:23.792
who never learned
not to meddle in people's lives.

617
00:49:26.072 --> 00:49:29.232
If you don't want to be a tenant,
sell this place,

618
00:49:29.352 --> 00:49:31.872
we can demolish the house
and build apartments.

619
00:49:31.992 --> 00:49:33.312
Parviz...

620
00:49:33.592 --> 00:49:36.592
the house is falling apart on all sides.

621
00:49:36.712 --> 00:49:38.952
We can't use it to build anything.

622
00:49:39.072 --> 00:49:42.392
We're in an urban decay area,
we don't pay taxes.

623
00:49:42.512 --> 00:49:45.272
We can build four stories,
with no elevator,

624
00:49:45.392 --> 00:49:47.392
and have a 590 sq. ft unit each.

625
00:49:47.752 --> 00:49:49.872
And with an elevator, Mr. Architect?

626
00:49:49.992 --> 00:49:53.392
With an elevator and standard staircase,
430 sq. ft each.

627
00:49:54.552 --> 00:49:56.272
Four units for the four of you.

628
00:49:56.392 --> 00:49:59.192
Just bury me and the parents
underneath it all.

629
00:49:59.312 --> 00:50:03.432
Know what? I'll live in the parking lot
with my kids, okay?

630
00:50:03.552 --> 00:50:04.872
Hold on...

631
00:50:05.832 --> 00:50:07.552
What if we take out a loan?

632
00:50:07.952 --> 00:50:10.072
We won't get one on the house.

633
00:50:10.192 --> 00:50:12.592
Get them out, please.
They're pissing me off.

634
00:50:12.712 --> 00:50:16.752
The walls could've collapsed.
We'd all be dead.

635
00:50:16.872 --> 00:50:19.792
Thank God,
you're here, fit as a fiddle

636
00:50:19.912 --> 00:50:22.952
in augmented reality
right before my eyes.

637
00:50:23.072 --> 00:50:26.472
Now that you're so elegant, can you eat?

638
00:50:26.592 --> 00:50:30.992
Elegance is fifteen people
all talking with their mouths full.

639
00:50:31.152 --> 00:50:35.352
How can you let your family
live in that house?

640
00:50:35.472 --> 00:50:39.792
You don't care about the family.
You just wanna be a homeowner.

641
00:50:39.912 --> 00:50:42.392
Can you build a house with no money?

642
00:50:48.112 --> 00:50:50.952
If we have the money,
we might as well buy the shop.

643
00:50:51.072 --> 00:50:54.832
- Finally.
- He sells his apartment, we buy the shop...

644
00:50:54.952 --> 00:50:58.792
- I got it. You're repeating yourself.
- Fine, I'll shut up.

645
00:50:58.912 --> 00:51:00.232
I'll think about it.

646
00:51:00.552 --> 00:51:04.792
If it's yes, I'll tell you.
If I say nothing, it's no.

647
00:51:06.152 --> 00:51:08.752
Don't eat that,
it's past the use-by date.

648
00:51:08.872 --> 00:51:10.992
It's still good to eat.

649
00:51:11.112 --> 00:51:13.792
You won't give us the apartment
or my passport?

650
00:51:15.392 --> 00:51:17.792
- I'm talking to you.
- Planning to use it?

651
00:51:18.392 --> 00:51:19.712
Did you hear him?

652
00:51:23.432 --> 00:51:25.272
Stop, give me that.

653
00:51:25.392 --> 00:51:28.792
- The combination?
- I'll ask him.

654
00:51:30.512 --> 00:51:32.152
What the hell are you doing?

655
00:51:32.272 --> 00:51:34.072
Are you out of your mind?

656
00:51:34.192 --> 00:51:36.992
- He'll give it back.
- What's he doing?

657
00:51:37.672 --> 00:51:40.792
If we don't get this dump,
he doesn't get my passport!

658
00:51:42.432 --> 00:51:45.792
What're you doing?
Leave my attaché case alone!

659
00:51:45.912 --> 00:51:47.592
Gimme that!

660
00:51:47.712 --> 00:51:49.432
What're you doing with my ID?

661
00:51:49.552 --> 00:51:51.192
It's not in there!

662
00:51:54.752 --> 00:51:57.192
I'll give it to you!

663
00:51:58.952 --> 00:52:01.992
You idiot! Let him give it to you!

664
00:52:02.112 --> 00:52:04.392
Gimme two seconds!

665
00:52:05.232 --> 00:52:06.752
Give me back my documents!

666
00:52:06.872 --> 00:52:09.832
Let him open it for you!

667
00:52:09.952 --> 00:52:12.472
- Give it back!
- Stop it!

668
00:52:13.032 --> 00:52:14.992
Give it back, you big bully!

669
00:52:15.512 --> 00:52:17.392
Why're you smashing it?

670
00:52:19.032 --> 00:52:20.832
What're you doing?

671
00:52:21.512 --> 00:52:23.112
Don't do that!

672
00:52:32.312 --> 00:52:34.392
Does he eat them or sell them?

673
00:52:42.992 --> 00:52:45.392
Why'd he do that?

674
00:52:58.432 --> 00:53:00.192
Can you type this up?

675
00:53:01.312 --> 00:53:02.632
Quiet, she's coming.

676
00:53:03.352 --> 00:53:04.992
Sorry to keep you waiting.

677
00:53:05.112 --> 00:53:09.112
- Hello.
- I presented your case to the board,

678
00:53:09.232 --> 00:53:12.952
using Ms. Jourablou's request

679
00:53:13.072 --> 00:53:16.352
in the hope of getting
the answer I wanted.

680
00:53:16.472 --> 00:53:23.392
In short, you need to put up 40% of the price
and obtain a 4-year loan to buy the shop.

681
00:53:23.552 --> 00:53:25.192
That gives us...

682
00:53:26.832 --> 00:53:30.592
Our deposit would have to be 176 million.

683
00:53:32.272 --> 00:53:34.472
Mr. Elias will see the details with you.

684
00:53:34.592 --> 00:53:36.352
When is the delivery date?

685
00:53:36.472 --> 00:53:39.992
In seven months.
Construction starts in three.

686
00:53:41.992 --> 00:53:43.912
Are your documents in order?

687
00:53:44.032 --> 00:53:47.352
No, we need some time to...

688
00:53:47.472 --> 00:53:50.792
- It won't take long.
- Can we have a few days?

689
00:53:52.072 --> 00:53:54.592
You handle it, Ms. Jourablou.

690
00:53:54.872 --> 00:53:56.792
- Thank you very much.
- You're welcome.

691
00:53:57.752 --> 00:53:59.992
Thank you very much. Bye.

692
00:54:00.392 --> 00:54:01.712
Thanks.

693
00:54:02.472 --> 00:54:03.792
You're welcome.

694
00:54:13.672 --> 00:54:16.672
Have a look around, see if you like it.

695
00:54:16.792 --> 00:54:19.392
I'm going to walk around, too.

696
00:54:38.712 --> 00:54:41.192
Come look at the fancy shops.

697
00:54:58.552 --> 00:55:01.992
Without a loan, we'll never get anywhere.

698
00:55:02.192 --> 00:55:03.792
Pitch in your apartment.

699
00:55:04.352 --> 00:55:05.672
Farhad, come here.

700
00:55:06.832 --> 00:55:10.592
Give my apartment a rest.
It wouldn't solve your problem.

701
00:55:11.672 --> 00:55:14.512
- We did the numbers.
- Yeah, but there's a hitch.

702
00:55:14.632 --> 00:55:16.792
I can only get 50,000 for my place.

703
00:55:17.632 --> 00:55:21.192
By pooling our money,
we only have 100, and we need 180.

704
00:55:22.952 --> 00:55:26.192
- What's the hitch?
- I have debts, nothing serious.

705
00:55:28.992 --> 00:55:31.792
What's wrong? You don't look well.

706
00:55:41.792 --> 00:55:44.192
Mehrnaz took a third of the apartment
for alimony.

707
00:55:47.912 --> 00:55:50.192
- For alimony?
- Yes.

708
00:55:52.392 --> 00:55:53.992
You divorced?

709
00:55:56.272 --> 00:55:57.992
Two months ago.

710
00:56:01.632 --> 00:56:03.792
Here. All done?

711
00:56:05.712 --> 00:56:08.232
I'm gonna gobble you up.

712
00:56:08.352 --> 00:56:09.992
- Parviz?
- Yes.

713
00:56:12.432 --> 00:56:13.992
How are you?

714
00:56:14.792 --> 00:56:16.112
Good to see you.

715
00:56:16.632 --> 00:56:18.392
How are things?

716
00:56:18.512 --> 00:56:22.512
Hello, young ladies.
Look how beautiful they are.

717
00:56:22.632 --> 00:56:25.392
- You okay?
- Sorry, went down the wrong way.

718
00:56:25.512 --> 00:56:27.112
You never stop by.

719
00:56:27.232 --> 00:56:28.712
I'm busy, as you see.

720
00:56:28.832 --> 00:56:30.992
God be with you.
Is your father home?

721
00:56:31.192 --> 00:56:32.512
My father?

722
00:56:32.632 --> 00:56:33.952
You want to see him?

723
00:56:34.472 --> 00:56:36.792
He must be home.

724
00:57:02.552 --> 00:57:03.872
Put them here.

725
00:57:04.872 --> 00:57:06.792
You should come inside, Esmail.

726
00:57:06.912 --> 00:57:08.232
We'll be outside.

727
00:57:08.512 --> 00:57:10.592
- Is the barbecue ready?
- Yes.

728
00:57:10.912 --> 00:57:14.392
- Jafar... Brew some tea.
- Alright.

729
00:57:14.792 --> 00:57:18.392
Get everyone out,
we need some time alone.

730
00:57:18.592 --> 00:57:19.912
Will do.

731
00:57:22.312 --> 00:57:25.992
Ehsan, sister, go on. I'll finish up.

732
00:57:26.432 --> 00:57:30.272
Why does your family
keep saying we hooked you on opium?

733
00:57:30.392 --> 00:57:34.632
It's jealousy.
We get along, so people talk.

734
00:57:34.752 --> 00:57:38.272
Not one of your sons
came to Gholam's memorial.

735
00:57:38.392 --> 00:57:41.592
- I'm sorry.
- That's all you can say.

736
00:57:42.112 --> 00:57:43.592
Jafar, bring the card.

737
00:57:44.512 --> 00:57:45.832
Listen, Cousin...

738
00:57:47.712 --> 00:57:52.192
A lot of people would love
to be named patriarch of the family.

739
00:57:53.232 --> 00:57:55.952
At my son's wedding,
Gholam's only grandson,

740
00:57:56.072 --> 00:57:57.992
we'll officially name a successor.

741
00:57:58.152 --> 00:57:59.592
Who would you choose?

742
00:57:59.992 --> 00:58:01.672
Ghardashali, of course.

743
00:58:01.792 --> 00:58:06.792
He's a gambler. His bad reputation
ultimately rubbed off on my father.

744
00:58:06.912 --> 00:58:09.112
True, but we have no choice.

745
00:58:09.232 --> 00:58:13.192
In his will, my father named you.

746
00:58:13.992 --> 00:58:15.312
Me?

747
00:58:15.712 --> 00:58:17.032
Why?

748
00:58:17.312 --> 00:58:20.392
You're the eldest
and you've always been loyal.

749
00:58:20.512 --> 00:58:22.032
That lot you gave him,

750
00:58:22.152 --> 00:58:23.792
he talked about it all the time.

751
00:58:23.912 --> 00:58:25.632
It was my duty.

752
00:58:25.752 --> 00:58:28.352
Which is why you deserve to be patriarch.

753
00:58:28.472 --> 00:58:30.392
Everyone will kowtow to you.

754
00:58:30.992 --> 00:58:32.792
I mean no disrespect,

755
00:58:32.992 --> 00:58:36.192
but do you have the shoulders
to sit in Gholam's place?

756
00:58:36.312 --> 00:58:37.792
I assure you I don't.

757
00:58:38.312 --> 00:58:39.632
You'll have to.

758
00:58:41.592 --> 00:58:42.992
Give me a straight answer:

759
00:58:43.392 --> 00:58:44.712
yes or no?

760
00:58:45.072 --> 00:58:46.592
Yes, of course.

761
00:58:47.832 --> 00:58:49.152
You feel up to it?

762
00:58:49.592 --> 00:58:52.272
I'm no great like you,
but I can emulate you.

763
00:58:52.392 --> 00:58:54.832
At the wedding,
you'll give the biggest gift.

764
00:58:54.952 --> 00:58:56.512
Do you have the means?

765
00:58:56.672 --> 00:58:58.472
I would do anything for you.

766
00:58:58.592 --> 00:59:00.192
You know the rules?

767
00:59:00.592 --> 00:59:03.592
The gift can only be cash or...

768
00:59:03.712 --> 00:59:05.432
Gold coins.

769
00:59:05.712 --> 00:59:07.952
- Do you have the money?
- I'll find it.

770
00:59:08.072 --> 00:59:10.192
- No.
- You have it or you'll find it?

771
00:59:11.472 --> 00:59:14.992
- I have it.
- You have to sign before a notary.

772
00:59:15.112 --> 00:59:16.472
With pleasure.

773
00:59:16.592 --> 00:59:18.392
I'm counting on that money.

774
00:59:18.512 --> 00:59:20.712
If you don't have it,
I'll ask someone else.

775
00:59:20.832 --> 00:59:24.312
- On my Gholam's life I have it.
- Your Gholam?

776
00:59:24.432 --> 00:59:26.312
Parviz just had a boy.

777
00:59:26.432 --> 00:59:29.192
We named him Gholam
in honor of your father.

778
00:59:31.752 --> 00:59:33.312
I've always said it,

779
00:59:33.432 --> 00:59:35.792
you're the most decent man in this family.

780
00:59:36.552 --> 00:59:41.792
Here, the list of gifts patriarchs have given
over the past 20 years.

781
00:59:41.952 --> 00:59:45.912
It goes up with each new wedding.

782
00:59:46.032 --> 00:59:51.192
I don't know what I've done
to deserve such an honor.

783
00:59:52.192 --> 00:59:53.512
You deserve it, Cousin.

784
00:59:54.952 --> 00:59:56.272
You deserve it.

785
00:59:57.872 --> 01:00:01.792
I should be kissing the ground you walk on.

786
01:00:08.792 --> 01:00:11.632
Why repeat what your shrew of a daughter says?

787
01:00:11.752 --> 01:00:13.952
How can you become patriarch?

788
01:00:14.072 --> 01:00:16.112
With the money she confiscated.

789
01:00:16.232 --> 01:00:19.312
- How much is that?
- Enough to become patriarch.

790
01:00:19.432 --> 01:00:22.352
You had the foresight to save up?

791
01:00:22.472 --> 01:00:25.592
Wouldn't you like us
to be patriarch and matriarch?

792
01:00:25.712 --> 01:00:29.432
Have everyone stand up
when we walk in a room?

793
01:00:29.552 --> 01:00:32.952
Will I be treated with great pomp
at Bayram's son's wedding?

794
01:00:33.072 --> 01:00:34.392
Of course!

795
01:00:34.592 --> 01:00:38.392
The day of the wedding,
they'll deliver our outfits.

796
01:00:39.112 --> 01:00:41.712
You'll be sitting next to the bride,

797
01:00:41.832 --> 01:00:44.032
and I'll sit next to the groom.

798
01:00:44.152 --> 01:00:47.952
The bride will ask for your permission
to say "I do."

799
01:00:48.072 --> 01:00:50.672
What if she doesn't and humiliates me?

800
01:00:50.792 --> 01:00:52.512
She can't, it's the law.

801
01:00:52.632 --> 01:00:56.192
I can't see those people
treating us that well.

802
01:00:56.312 --> 01:00:57.792
That's nothing.

803
01:00:58.112 --> 01:01:03.192
When I die, the announcement will read:
"Patriarch of the Jourablou Clan."

804
01:01:03.312 --> 01:01:05.992
And for you, it'll read,

805
01:01:06.112 --> 01:01:08.872
"Wife of the Patriarch of the Jourablou Clan."

806
01:01:08.992 --> 01:01:11.552
They didn't even use to say hello.

807
01:01:11.672 --> 01:01:14.312
Why would they make you this offer?

808
01:01:14.432 --> 01:01:16.432
First of all, I'm the eldest.

809
01:01:16.552 --> 01:01:18.512
Second of all, it was in Gholam's will.

810
01:01:18.632 --> 01:01:20.512
He named you in his will?

811
01:01:20.632 --> 01:01:22.392
I'm telling you!

812
01:01:22.752 --> 01:01:25.792
Teach your children to respect the family.

813
01:01:26.272 --> 01:01:30.992
You know what will change for us,
if I become patriarch.

814
01:01:31.112 --> 01:01:34.792
And what it'll change for the others!

815
01:01:38.632 --> 01:01:42.912
Farhad... What?

816
01:01:43.032 --> 01:01:47.192
Dad's decided to impress Bayram
at his son's wedding.

817
01:01:47.352 --> 01:01:50.792
Promising. Just what we needed!

818
01:01:56.072 --> 01:01:58.712
What're you and your husband up to again?

819
01:01:58.832 --> 01:02:01.712
- Isn't my husband your father?
- That's for you to say.

820
01:02:01.832 --> 01:02:03.152
Dad, what's up?

821
01:02:03.512 --> 01:02:07.792
We're invited to the wedding.
I'm being named patriarch.

822
01:02:09.712 --> 01:02:11.272
We're screwed. He's loving this.

823
01:02:11.392 --> 01:02:13.832
Don't you like being respected?

824
01:02:13.952 --> 01:02:15.472
Nobody dislikes it.

825
01:02:15.592 --> 01:02:18.312
But isn't this sudden respect suspicious?

826
01:02:18.432 --> 01:02:22.192
Do you know Gholam
paid the mortgage on this house?

827
01:02:22.832 --> 01:02:28.392
How can you tell such huge lies
to your own detriment?

828
01:02:28.592 --> 01:02:31.512
The more they disdain you,
the more you idolize them.

829
01:02:31.632 --> 01:02:33.392
What have they ever done for you?

830
01:02:33.512 --> 01:02:36.952
They made a junky of you at 70
to steal your inheritance!

831
01:02:37.072 --> 01:02:38.472
Don't be ridiculous.

832
01:02:38.592 --> 01:02:40.632
For two acres of arid land...

833
01:02:40.752 --> 01:02:43.632
That're worth 100 million today!

834
01:02:43.752 --> 01:02:48.992
Gholam and Bayram
spent ten times more on me by the sea.

835
01:02:49.432 --> 01:02:52.392
You want to talk me out of it?

836
01:02:52.792 --> 01:02:54.792
What kind of a phone call was that?

837
01:02:54.912 --> 01:02:57.392
I'm going out of my mind.

838
01:02:57.512 --> 01:03:01.432
Dad's invited to the wedding as patriarch,
so he's giving the first gift,

839
01:03:01.552 --> 01:03:03.752
the most expensive one.

840
01:03:03.872 --> 01:03:07.192
- He can just give a small one.
- He can't.

841
01:03:07.312 --> 01:03:11.232
The patriarch's gift has to be the biggest.

842
01:03:11.352 --> 01:03:15.472
If he gives a small one,
the others will be tiny.

843
01:03:15.592 --> 01:03:17.512
Think of the hosts.

844
01:03:17.632 --> 01:03:20.232
Alireza, when I got married,

845
01:03:20.352 --> 01:03:23.912
I was humiliated
by those asshole cousins of his.

846
01:03:24.032 --> 01:03:25.592
Shame on you.

847
01:03:27.232 --> 01:03:29.272
What about the coins Gholam gave you?

848
01:03:29.392 --> 01:03:32.352
How can you say that in front of us?

849
01:03:32.472 --> 01:03:34.872
Gholam didn't even want to come
to his wedding!

850
01:03:34.992 --> 01:03:37.912
Dad had to buy 5 coins on credit.

851
01:03:38.032 --> 01:03:41.792
Gholam deigned to come gift them
as if he were generous.

852
01:03:41.912 --> 01:03:45.872
That wedding was the worst night of my life!

853
01:03:45.992 --> 01:03:49.072
We expected 300 guests, there weren't 50.

854
01:03:49.192 --> 01:03:52.032
At 1 a.m., people were leaving
and I was still hoping

855
01:03:52.152 --> 01:03:54.392
your relatives would show up.

856
01:03:54.512 --> 01:03:57.752
I have a list of the gifts exchanged
these past 20 years.

857
01:03:57.872 --> 01:04:00.432
This notebook holds proof of their ploys.

858
01:04:00.552 --> 01:04:02.592
How much was Gholam's last gift?

859
01:04:02.712 --> 01:04:04.312
For his granddaughter, 30.

860
01:04:04.432 --> 01:04:07.872
This time, Bayram,
the groom's father, is giving 35.

861
01:04:07.992 --> 01:04:09.992
So they expect Dad to pay 40!

862
01:04:10.432 --> 01:04:11.752
40 what?

863
01:04:11.872 --> 01:04:13.232
40 gold coins?

864
01:04:13.352 --> 01:04:16.832
Everything's bogus,
the bride's name, the gifts...

865
01:04:16.952 --> 01:04:18.912
Why should we give them real gold?

866
01:04:19.032 --> 01:04:21.592
You're losing your marbles.

867
01:04:21.712 --> 01:04:24.272
There were one or two missteps.

868
01:04:24.392 --> 01:04:27.272
Bayram doesn't have enough
to throw a wedding.

869
01:04:27.392 --> 01:04:29.152
That's why he's come to you.

870
01:04:29.272 --> 01:04:32.312
He came out of respect for our traditions.

871
01:04:32.432 --> 01:04:35.592
I am both the eldest and the chosen one.

872
01:04:35.712 --> 01:04:39.072
- Stop bothering me.
- Dig your head out of the sand.

873
01:04:39.192 --> 01:04:43.072
You know the first gift's a set up.

874
01:04:43.192 --> 01:04:47.232
No millionaire gives as big a gift
as our dirt-poor patriarch.

875
01:04:47.352 --> 01:04:51.272
Mom. How did he get you
to shut up about this?

876
01:04:51.392 --> 01:04:53.792
Her? She thinks she's a queen now.

877
01:04:53.952 --> 01:04:59.072
Tell me, my queen! Haven't you spent your life
talking behind his family's back?

878
01:04:59.192 --> 01:05:02.792
You've always wanted to cut off all ties.

879
01:05:03.032 --> 01:05:05.592
They've changed, that's all!

880
01:05:05.912 --> 01:05:09.232
They've always benefited
from mistreating people.

881
01:05:09.352 --> 01:05:11.192
They'll never change!

882
01:05:11.312 --> 01:05:14.152
At every wedding,
Gholam would take a dozen coins,

883
01:05:14.272 --> 01:05:19.152
pocket 5 and give the rest as a gift.
And everyone was happy to see him.

884
01:05:19.272 --> 01:05:21.392
There! He knows what he's saying!

885
01:05:21.512 --> 01:05:24.072
Ask them to lend you 40 coins

886
01:05:24.192 --> 01:05:27.392
and give them back
while passing for the highest bidder.

887
01:05:29.312 --> 01:05:30.632
What're you doing?

888
01:05:31.072 --> 01:05:35.232
- Are you running away?
- Don't be so hard. Think of his heart.

889
01:05:35.352 --> 01:05:37.872
- Step aside.
- Alireza, son...

890
01:05:37.992 --> 01:05:40.592
- Let them talk.
- Can we have an answer?

891
01:05:40.712 --> 01:05:44.712
If they wanted to foot the bill,
they wouldn't have opened the door.

892
01:05:44.832 --> 01:05:46.672
You know and you're going?

893
01:05:46.792 --> 01:05:50.592
It won't work with Bayram,
but it will with future weddings.

894
01:05:50.712 --> 01:05:55.392
The rest of my life, I'll pocket a percentage
and give them the rest.

895
01:05:55.592 --> 01:06:00.912
Everyone knows it's a scam
but they gladly take part in it?

896
01:06:01.032 --> 01:06:05.312
Yes, it's a cycle.
They know they'll have their turn.

897
01:06:05.432 --> 01:06:09.192
It's always been.
With all the weddings planned,

898
01:06:09.312 --> 01:06:11.312
if Dad's smart, he'll make some dough.

899
01:06:11.432 --> 01:06:14.552
You're dumb enough to think he's smart?

900
01:06:14.672 --> 01:06:17.792
Of course I'm smart.
I'm just as good as they are.

901
01:06:17.912 --> 01:06:20.432
I took the bus to work for 37 years.

902
01:06:20.552 --> 01:06:22.752
Proof you're not so smart.

903
01:06:22.872 --> 01:06:25.272
You slaved away your whole life.

904
01:06:25.392 --> 01:06:27.592
You were never a freeloader.

905
01:06:27.712 --> 01:06:31.072
Every time they show up in our lives,
they bring trouble.

906
01:06:31.192 --> 01:06:33.152
We can't give you the money.

907
01:06:33.272 --> 01:06:35.912
We're starting a business.

908
01:06:36.032 --> 01:06:38.792
- Whose money were you counting on?
- Mine!

909
01:06:39.072 --> 01:06:40.992
- What do you have?
- Gold coins!

910
01:06:41.112 --> 01:06:44.232
- How many?
- 40! You tell them!

911
01:06:44.352 --> 01:06:48.392
He's delirious. It's withdrawal.
Go get your hit.

912
01:06:48.552 --> 01:06:49.872
What's he talking about, Leila?

913
01:06:50.072 --> 01:06:53.752
It's true. That's why I called you.

914
01:06:53.872 --> 01:06:56.192
- How many does he have?
- 40.

915
01:06:56.512 --> 01:06:59.192
40 coins.

916
01:06:59.392 --> 01:07:02.232
- Where'd you get them?
- I had them.

917
01:07:02.352 --> 01:07:05.032
You had 40 coins and we didn't know?

918
01:07:05.152 --> 01:07:07.992
- You'd have taken them.
- Really?

919
01:07:08.192 --> 01:07:11.512
You've watched us struggle
without saying anything?

920
01:07:11.632 --> 01:07:14.712
It was my nest egg, for a rainy day.

921
01:07:14.832 --> 01:07:16.672
Every day is a rainy day!

922
01:07:16.792 --> 01:07:19.552
Leila, how much more
do we need for the shop?

923
01:07:19.672 --> 01:07:21.392
- 60 million.
- Manouchehr?

924
01:07:21.512 --> 01:07:23.792
- That's correct.
- Parviz, Farhad...

925
01:07:23.952 --> 01:07:28.392
See, Dad? With your coins,
we could buy that shop.

926
01:07:28.512 --> 01:07:34.192
- You all talk, but you don't listen!
- And that way, we'd all have jobs.

927
01:07:34.352 --> 01:07:37.832
All our problems would be solved.

928
01:07:37.952 --> 01:07:41.792
We could start our own families.

929
01:07:41.912 --> 01:07:44.392
And you would be our patriarch.

930
01:07:44.512 --> 01:07:46.312
All with a single shop.

931
01:07:46.432 --> 01:07:50.992
These coins aren't for a shop.
They're for a wedding I'm the patriarch of.

932
01:07:51.112 --> 01:07:53.552
- Dad...
- Leave me alone!

933
01:07:53.672 --> 01:07:55.992
If you're not happy, get out!

934
01:07:56.152 --> 01:07:57.992
- Excuse me?
- Give me that!

935
01:07:58.152 --> 01:08:00.552
- What do I do?
- They're mine! Don't ask him!

936
01:08:00.672 --> 01:08:02.032
Hand them over!

937
01:08:02.232 --> 01:08:04.512
Here. Do you hear yourself?

938
01:08:04.632 --> 01:08:07.072
Ghardashali would give anything
to be in my shoes.

939
01:08:07.192 --> 01:08:09.952
- Because he's dumb!
- I'm dumber than he is!

940
01:08:10.072 --> 01:08:11.552
Money comes and goes.

941
01:08:11.672 --> 01:08:16.552
Your dad dreams of being honored
for once in his life.

942
01:08:16.672 --> 01:08:21.112
Mom, your four sons are unemployed.

943
01:08:21.232 --> 01:08:23.952
They dream of having stable jobs.

944
01:08:24.072 --> 01:08:29.352
Dad, your sons have no money,
no health insurance,

945
01:08:29.472 --> 01:08:33.192
and no hope of one day having a pension.

946
01:08:33.592 --> 01:08:34.912
Dad...

947
01:08:36.472 --> 01:08:37.792
Dad.

948
01:08:38.152 --> 01:08:39.472
Look at me.

949
01:08:40.272 --> 01:08:41.592
Daddy dearest,

950
01:08:42.152 --> 01:08:44.392
you know what I'm afraid of?

951
01:08:44.512 --> 01:08:45.992
Don't take this badly.

952
01:08:46.832 --> 01:08:50.032
I'm afraid that,
if we give them 40 coins,

953
01:08:50.152 --> 01:08:54.192
they'll say the coins were theirs.

954
01:08:54.792 --> 01:08:57.192
Everyone will believe them.

955
01:08:58.512 --> 01:08:59.832
You know why?

956
01:09:00.472 --> 01:09:05.272
Because we don't look like
we can give 40 coins or 50 million.

957
01:09:05.392 --> 01:09:07.792
We're just too poor.

958
01:09:08.992 --> 01:09:10.312
Really.

959
01:09:11.192 --> 01:09:12.912
He's right.

960
01:09:13.472 --> 01:09:18.072
We'd be better off renting out our suits,

961
01:09:18.192 --> 01:09:22.392
than giving a gift that's so pricey
we'll be suspected and ridiculed.

962
01:09:22.712 --> 01:09:25.592
I don't want to argue with you.

963
01:09:25.792 --> 01:09:28.592
But they're leading you up the garden path.

964
01:09:28.952 --> 01:09:30.592
That path is a street.

965
01:09:31.192 --> 01:09:32.512
An avenue.

966
01:09:32.672 --> 01:09:33.992
A boulevard,

967
01:09:34.272 --> 01:09:36.192
a royal boulevard.

968
01:09:45.392 --> 01:09:47.672
- Dad!
- Oh, my goodness!

969
01:09:47.792 --> 01:09:49.112
Dad!

970
01:09:49.792 --> 01:09:52.752
Get him up. Alireza, Farhad...

971
01:09:52.872 --> 01:09:54.192
Calm down.

972
01:09:55.272 --> 01:09:57.792
- Dad...
- Is he breathing?

973
01:09:58.472 --> 01:09:59.792
Daddy dearest.

974
01:10:00.712 --> 01:10:03.992
Wait over there.
The IV will be finished 30 minutes.

975
01:10:10.512 --> 01:10:12.992
The IV will be finished in 30 minutes.

976
01:10:16.632 --> 01:10:19.392
Did you know Dad's never been by the sea?

977
01:10:19.592 --> 01:10:23.592
- He said he went with Gholam...
- A pack of lies.

978
01:10:24.032 --> 01:10:26.392
They never took him.

979
01:10:26.712 --> 01:10:30.192
When you can't feed your family,
you don't go on weekend getaways!

980
01:10:31.032 --> 01:10:36.392
He makes up memories with his cousins
to prove that they love him.

981
01:10:36.752 --> 01:10:39.592
For that bastard Bayram's wedding,

982
01:10:39.952 --> 01:10:43.592
Dad dry-cleaned his suit a month in advance.

983
01:10:43.792 --> 01:10:46.792
He checked the mail every day for the invite.

984
01:10:46.912 --> 01:10:48.232
It never came.

985
01:10:48.712 --> 01:10:50.032
He never went.

986
01:10:50.272 --> 01:10:54.192
But he's shared a thousand memories
of that wedding.

987
01:10:55.032 --> 01:10:59.992
He even says I was there,
and uses me as a witness.

988
01:11:00.512 --> 01:11:05.192
Being their guest of honor
means the world to him.

989
01:11:05.592 --> 01:11:07.592
So leave him alone.

990
01:11:08.192 --> 01:11:10.392
Let him do what he wants.

991
01:11:12.592 --> 01:11:16.792
He tried so hard to get their attention
that he got their pity.

992
01:11:16.912 --> 01:11:18.592
Not even.

993
01:11:18.712 --> 01:11:22.912
When that bastard Gholam was alive,
he wouldn't give him time of day.

994
01:11:23.032 --> 01:11:26.592
Now they expect us to believe
he named him in his will?

995
01:11:27.392 --> 01:11:29.792
I don't think there is a will.

996
01:11:30.152 --> 01:11:36.192
And if there is, it means we're letting
a dead man dictate our lives.

997
01:12:08.352 --> 01:12:10.072
What's gotten into you?

998
01:12:56.792 --> 01:12:58.192
What're you doing?

999
01:13:00.472 --> 01:13:02.392
The dishes can wait.

1000
01:13:02.792 --> 01:13:05.552
I'm cleaning your father's piss.

1001
01:13:05.672 --> 01:13:08.792
That's what you get for sneaking a smoke.

1002
01:13:10.152 --> 01:13:11.992
Who're you talking to?

1003
01:13:12.192 --> 01:13:14.872
Don't you mind seeing your sister smoke?

1004
01:13:14.992 --> 01:13:18.792
Didn't your brothers mind seeing you
6 months pregnant at your wedding?

1005
01:13:19.912 --> 01:13:22.832
Alireza, aren't you going to scold that hussy?

1006
01:13:22.952 --> 01:13:25.392
You're the one who was pregnant, not her.

1007
01:13:46.752 --> 01:13:49.392
I don't know what to do anymore.

1008
01:13:49.952 --> 01:13:55.592
Don't worry. Things can get worse
than this here. Then you forget.

1009
01:14:04.472 --> 01:14:06.912
For me? I don't smoke.

1010
01:14:07.032 --> 01:14:10.592
Take it. Smoke rarely
and quit when you can.

1011
01:14:21.872 --> 01:14:23.192
You alright?

1012
01:14:24.632 --> 01:14:26.792
- I'm okay.
- Are you sure?

1013
01:14:27.232 --> 01:14:29.592
- Yes.
- Are you lying?

1014
01:14:29.712 --> 01:14:31.032
Yes.

1015
01:14:34.072 --> 01:14:35.392
Don't worry.

1016
01:14:35.552 --> 01:14:39.192
Only when you hit rock bottom
do you learn how to get up.

1017
01:14:41.752 --> 01:14:43.592
Good thing you don't smoke.

1018
01:14:49.952 --> 01:14:51.992
You think Oshin's still alive?

1019
01:14:52.312 --> 01:14:54.032
Wanna get in touch?

1020
01:14:55.032 --> 01:14:56.592
If it wasn't for that TV show,

1021
01:14:56.712 --> 01:15:00.592
we'd never have known
we had to endure our miserable lives.

1022
01:15:00.712 --> 01:15:03.192
We don't endure them,
we improve them.

1023
01:15:03.472 --> 01:15:06.992
Even Oshin, with her thrift store,
improved their lives.

1024
01:15:07.592 --> 01:15:09.592
My brothers are a bunch of losers.

1025
01:15:09.752 --> 01:15:11.872
- Why?
- Even a thrift store's too much to ask.

1026
01:15:11.992 --> 01:15:13.312
True!

1027
01:15:22.712 --> 01:15:25.992
I still don't understand
how we sank so low.

1028
01:15:27.032 --> 01:15:30.592
It's not at all the future
I envisioned as a kid.

1029
01:15:32.032 --> 01:15:36.992
I've learned that growing up
means slowly but surely

1030
01:15:37.392 --> 01:15:40.792
giving up on what you want.

1031
01:15:43.992 --> 01:15:46.792
Did you know that all the rich people
know each other?

1032
01:15:47.152 --> 01:15:49.792
- I see it at work.
- Why?

1033
01:15:51.312 --> 01:15:52.632
There aren't many of them.

1034
01:15:53.592 --> 01:15:58.392
Poor people don't know each other,
they recognize each other.

1035
01:15:59.592 --> 01:16:01.392
I don't know. Maybe.

1036
01:16:04.352 --> 01:16:07.192
You had a suitor who disappeared...

1037
01:16:07.632 --> 01:16:09.192
- Majid.
- Yeah.

1038
01:16:09.672 --> 01:16:11.592
Did you know he got divorced?

1039
01:16:11.792 --> 01:16:13.112
So what?

1040
01:16:13.752 --> 01:16:15.792
Do you still like him?

1041
01:16:16.712 --> 01:16:18.752
I'd forgotten he existed.

1042
01:16:18.912 --> 01:16:20.392
Thank God.

1043
01:16:21.312 --> 01:16:24.792
- Why?
- He just married his second wife.

1044
01:16:26.152 --> 01:16:29.792
Third time's the charm.
He'll come after me next.

1045
01:16:30.032 --> 01:16:32.192
Practice makes perfect.

1046
01:16:34.672 --> 01:16:37.112
Why'd he disappear all of a sudden?

1047
01:16:37.232 --> 01:16:40.592
Dad told him I had an illness.

1048
01:16:40.792 --> 01:16:42.952
- Who told you?
- Majid did.

1049
01:16:43.072 --> 01:16:45.792
- When?
- After his divorce.

1050
01:16:45.912 --> 01:16:48.592
- You're still in touch?
- He called me once

1051
01:16:48.712 --> 01:16:50.392
to suggest we get together.

1052
01:16:50.552 --> 01:16:51.872
I said no.

1053
01:16:57.392 --> 01:16:59.992
Why would Dad say such a thing?

1054
01:17:00.392 --> 01:17:03.072
He wanted me to marry
someone from his family.

1055
01:17:03.192 --> 01:17:07.552
- Did you want to?
- I never got a chance to give my opinion.

1056
01:17:07.672 --> 01:17:08.992
What do you mean?

1057
01:17:09.112 --> 01:17:14.592
Dad tried to charm them
into sending a suitor to marry me.

1058
01:17:14.752 --> 01:17:16.792
None of them wanted me.

1059
01:17:22.512 --> 01:17:24.592
What can I do to help pull us out of this?

1060
01:17:29.792 --> 01:17:31.512
Have a magic lantern?

1061
01:17:31.792 --> 01:17:33.112
Suppose I did.

1062
01:17:34.952 --> 01:17:36.792
Give me a sister.

1063
01:17:37.232 --> 01:17:40.792
An older one, that I can lean on.

1064
01:17:42.552 --> 01:17:43.872
And?

1065
01:17:44.032 --> 01:17:45.352
And...

1066
01:17:46.112 --> 01:17:49.792
Take Manouchehr back to his school days,
when he was so smart.

1067
01:17:51.552 --> 01:17:54.152
- Is that all?
- Make us forget this period

1068
01:17:54.272 --> 01:17:55.952
with the wave of a magic wand.

1069
01:17:56.072 --> 01:17:57.792
Me or the magic lantern?

1070
01:17:57.912 --> 01:18:00.792
- If only you could.
- If I could...

1071
01:18:03.312 --> 01:18:05.992
I'd buy a shop for each of us.

1072
01:18:07.552 --> 01:18:09.672
And I'd make Dad our patriarch.

1073
01:18:09.792 --> 01:18:11.992
Luckily, your wishes can come true.

1074
01:18:12.112 --> 01:18:15.432
- How?
- We stop Dad from going to the wedding

1075
01:18:15.552 --> 01:18:18.592
- and we buy the shop.
- Have you lost your mind?

1076
01:18:19.152 --> 01:18:21.632
He just got out of the hospital.

1077
01:18:21.752 --> 01:18:24.072
He passed out for real, this time.

1078
01:18:24.192 --> 01:18:25.792
I don't believe it.

1079
01:18:26.312 --> 01:18:29.312
You want him to give them the coins
at the wedding?

1080
01:18:29.432 --> 01:18:32.632
I want nothing.
I'm saying they're his to give.

1081
01:18:32.752 --> 01:18:35.792
It's either the wedding or the shop.

1082
01:18:35.912 --> 01:18:37.992
It's his life or his death.

1083
01:18:38.152 --> 01:18:42.072
Another fight like that one
and he's sure to have a heart attack.

1084
01:18:42.192 --> 01:18:44.192
And you'll take care of him.

1085
01:18:44.352 --> 01:18:47.192
- Drop it, Leila.
- I can't drop it.

1086
01:18:47.592 --> 01:18:48.912
And you have no right to!

1087
01:18:49.032 --> 01:18:54.792
I agree that it's a poor decision.
But poor decision-making is what he does.

1088
01:18:55.072 --> 01:18:56.592
He's like a stubborn kid.

1089
01:18:56.712 --> 01:18:58.832
That's all we have in this family.

1090
01:18:58.952 --> 01:19:01.912
Even the old folks are stubborn kids.

1091
01:19:02.032 --> 01:19:03.992
If we pressure him, he'll die.

1092
01:19:04.272 --> 01:19:07.592
- Is that your final word?
- It was also my first.

1093
01:19:07.712 --> 01:19:10.232
We're all free to do as we please.

1094
01:19:10.352 --> 01:19:13.152
We're all responsible for our own lives.

1095
01:19:13.272 --> 01:19:17.952
No one has the right to whine their way
into other people's lives.

1096
01:19:18.072 --> 01:19:20.592
Are you saying that for me?

1097
01:19:21.192 --> 01:19:23.392
Am I whining for myself?

1098
01:19:24.032 --> 01:19:25.712
I asked you to stay to help me.

1099
01:19:25.832 --> 01:19:29.592
If I stick around,
you'll have to listen to me.

1100
01:19:30.072 --> 01:19:32.392
If you act like the others I'll leave.

1101
01:19:45.952 --> 01:19:49.792
Mom! Heat up my lunch.
I've got a ride, I'm late.

1102
01:20:04.112 --> 01:20:06.752
- You were out Saturday.
- I was looking for work.

1103
01:20:06.872 --> 01:20:09.552
You'll lose your benefits next time.

1104
01:20:09.672 --> 01:20:11.792
- Yes, sir.
- Let me see your ID.

1105
01:20:19.072 --> 01:20:22.992
Ali! Careful not to fall again.

1106
01:20:24.192 --> 01:20:27.992
Hurry up, Mommy. It's started.

1107
01:20:28.432 --> 01:20:29.752
Come on!

1108
01:20:35.352 --> 01:20:36.672
Hello.

1109
01:21:10.032 --> 01:21:12.192
Dad, get outta there!

1110
01:21:12.472 --> 01:21:15.192
- What's that?
- Bayram sent it for Dad.

1111
01:21:15.672 --> 01:21:17.512
There's no water again!

1112
01:21:17.632 --> 01:21:21.992
Mom, Leila, shut off the water.
We're all waiting to use the shower.

1113
01:21:22.112 --> 01:21:25.232
- Alireza?
- Beautiful! Is that for me?

1114
01:21:25.352 --> 01:21:26.672
It sure is.

1115
01:21:26.792 --> 01:21:28.152
Classy.

1116
01:21:28.272 --> 01:21:31.672
The shirt I promised you. Super XL!

1117
01:21:31.792 --> 01:21:34.312
Thanks very much, little brother!

1118
01:21:34.432 --> 01:21:36.872
These shoes go well with that suit.

1119
01:21:36.992 --> 01:21:39.392
- Thank you, Manouchehr.
- Don't mention it.

1120
01:21:39.512 --> 01:21:41.632
These watches are fake, but they work.

1121
01:21:41.752 --> 01:21:44.392
- Here, Parviz. Take one.
- Thanks.

1122
01:21:44.512 --> 01:21:47.152
Solid gold brothers!

1123
01:21:47.272 --> 01:21:48.592
- Manou-junk?
- Yes.

1124
01:21:48.712 --> 01:21:50.032
Can I take this?

1125
01:21:50.832 --> 01:21:53.592
- I've worn it once.
- I don't mind. I like it.

1126
01:21:53.752 --> 01:21:56.432
- Take it.
- Parviz, I took out the insoles,

1127
01:21:56.552 --> 01:21:58.992
- they should fit.
- Thank you.

1128
01:21:59.312 --> 01:22:02.592
Look at that peachy complexion!

1129
01:22:02.712 --> 01:22:04.752
Peach or tomato?

1130
01:22:04.872 --> 01:22:10.112
Neither peach nor tomato.
That's my little duckling.

1131
01:22:10.232 --> 01:22:12.752
I'm going to eat that little duckling.

1132
01:22:12.872 --> 01:22:14.592
You're handsome, Daddy dearest.

1133
01:22:14.712 --> 01:22:16.992
A true newlywed.

1134
01:22:17.312 --> 01:22:18.792
If you say so.

1135
01:22:18.912 --> 01:22:21.592
I hope that this year,
we can all go together

1136
01:22:21.712 --> 01:22:23.792
to the beautiful beaches in Pattaya.

1137
01:22:23.952 --> 01:22:25.992
I'm counting on you.

1138
01:22:26.152 --> 01:22:28.952
- Got the coins from Leila?
- She's gift-wrapping the box.

1139
01:22:29.072 --> 01:22:31.672
Make sure she wraps it beautifully.

1140
01:22:31.792 --> 01:22:35.032
- She will.
- Dad, Bayram sent you this.

1141
01:22:35.152 --> 01:22:38.672
- Fantastic.
- Alireza, can I go next?

1142
01:22:38.792 --> 01:22:41.312
- Yeah, don't take 3 hours.
- I'll make it quick.

1143
01:22:41.432 --> 01:22:46.792
A suit paid for by Bayram is something else.

1144
01:23:17.432 --> 01:23:21.192
Look how handsome they are!
May God keep you.

1145
01:23:21.392 --> 01:23:25.792
- Pray.
- Stop it, Mom. That's Parviz's meal.

1146
01:23:30.512 --> 01:23:32.072
Let me take your picture.

1147
01:23:32.192 --> 01:23:34.072
Mom, go stand next to him.

1148
01:23:34.192 --> 01:23:36.072
Manouchehr, next to Alireza.

1149
01:23:36.192 --> 01:23:38.872
- Farhad, on this side. You're taller.
- Careful.

1150
01:23:38.992 --> 01:23:41.592
I am. Line up. Parviz, step forward.

1151
01:23:41.792 --> 01:23:45.992
Come on, line up properly.
I am being careful.

1152
01:23:46.112 --> 01:23:48.152
Now. Look at me.

1153
01:23:48.272 --> 01:23:52.152
Very nice. More to the left.

1154
01:23:52.272 --> 01:23:54.472
I don't want the bathroom door.

1155
01:23:54.592 --> 01:23:56.592
More... Good.

1156
01:23:56.912 --> 01:23:58.992
One... Smile.

1157
01:23:59.112 --> 01:24:00.432
Two...

1158
01:24:00.912 --> 01:24:03.792
My sweethearts, you're gorgeous.

1159
01:24:05.192 --> 01:24:06.512
Three.

1160
01:24:08.552 --> 01:24:09.872
All done?

1161
01:24:11.592 --> 01:24:15.792
Leila, Dad's all dressed up.
Take a picture of him alone.

1162
01:24:15.912 --> 01:24:17.792
Take one of us two first.

1163
01:24:18.152 --> 01:24:20.392
Parviz, out of the way.
I want him alone.

1164
01:24:20.552 --> 01:24:22.472
Why? They look nice together.

1165
01:24:22.592 --> 01:24:26.072
- He doesn't have a nice portrait.
- Contradicting me again?

1166
01:24:26.192 --> 01:24:29.392
What do you want a portrait for?
Go on then.

1167
01:24:29.872 --> 01:24:33.592
We never know what might happen.

1168
01:24:34.472 --> 01:24:35.872
It's for his funeral.

1169
01:24:35.992 --> 01:24:38.792
Dad, come stand over here.

1170
01:24:39.912 --> 01:24:44.112
- Farhad, sit to pee!
- Don't, it's a bad omen.

1171
01:24:44.232 --> 01:24:46.392
- Don't take it.
- Death comes when it's ready.

1172
01:24:46.512 --> 01:24:48.232
Take one of me, too.

1173
01:24:48.552 --> 01:24:51.672
Give us a break.
We can't use your picture.

1174
01:24:51.792 --> 01:24:53.792
We'll have to use a flower! Move.

1175
01:24:55.392 --> 01:24:58.592
Leila, take it.
Tonight's photo is different.

1176
01:25:25.392 --> 01:25:27.672
Dad, should I hold it for you?

1177
01:25:27.792 --> 01:25:30.992
Give it to Bayram when it's gift time.

1178
01:25:31.112 --> 01:25:32.432
Okay.

1179
01:25:34.752 --> 01:25:36.072
Alireza?

1180
01:25:36.352 --> 01:25:37.672
Yes?

1181
01:25:37.912 --> 01:25:42.392
Thank you. If it weren't for you,
the others wouldn't have let me go.

1182
01:25:44.312 --> 01:25:46.192
Love you, Dad.

1183
01:25:55.912 --> 01:26:01.192
Hello, congratulations.
I wish them the best.

1184
01:26:02.792 --> 01:26:04.992
Hello. How are you?

1185
01:26:19.792 --> 01:26:23.472
Ladies, on the 2nd via the elevator.
Gentlemen, stairs to the 1st.

1186
01:26:23.592 --> 01:26:25.272
Hello. How are you?

1187
01:26:25.392 --> 01:26:27.192
Hello, welcome!

1188
01:26:27.432 --> 01:26:30.792
What a pleasure to see you!

1189
01:26:31.072 --> 01:26:33.192
Congratulations!

1190
01:26:38.312 --> 01:26:42.192
Welcome to this marvelous evening.

1191
01:26:42.352 --> 01:26:45.952
I want to hear your applause!

1192
01:26:46.072 --> 01:26:48.192
Ladies up there, too!

1193
01:26:55.832 --> 01:26:59.912
What an honor for me to name

1194
01:27:00.032 --> 01:27:03.992
the late Gholam Jourablou's
successor tonight.

1195
01:27:04.152 --> 01:27:05.752
Thank you!

1196
01:27:05.872 --> 01:27:08.192
What a great atmosphere!

1197
01:27:15.792 --> 01:27:19.272
Keep it up! No slowing down now!

1198
01:27:19.392 --> 01:27:21.392
We're in for a long night!

1199
01:27:22.992 --> 01:27:24.992
Thank you.

1200
01:27:25.672 --> 01:27:28.592
What a night!

1201
01:27:28.992 --> 01:27:32.592
And now the time has come
to name the patriarch.

1202
01:27:33.192 --> 01:27:37.592
On this day, in this hour,
in this glorious second,

1203
01:27:38.272 --> 01:27:39.912
the name of the patriarch

1204
01:27:40.032 --> 01:27:43.232
of the family born
of the dynasty of the Jourablou clan,

1205
01:27:43.352 --> 01:27:49.592
as wished by Gholam,
is now going to be officially announced.

1206
01:27:50.072 --> 01:27:52.832
And the name is Mr...

1207
01:27:52.952 --> 01:27:56.192
Esmail Jourablou!

1208
01:27:56.352 --> 01:28:00.792
Bring the house down with your applause!

1209
01:28:01.152 --> 01:28:06.232
I want to hear you until the end of the night!

1210
01:28:06.352 --> 01:28:10.592
Again and again, make more noise!

1211
01:28:11.072 --> 01:28:12.792
Classy!

1212
01:28:20.072 --> 01:28:25.232
Encourage him now!
Until the end of the night!

1213
01:28:25.352 --> 01:28:29.592
I want to hear each and every one of you!

1214
01:28:29.712 --> 01:28:32.392
Let's congratulate him!

1215
01:28:42.992 --> 01:28:45.392
You're not whistling loud enough!

1216
01:29:17.392 --> 01:29:19.392
Congratulations, my boy.

1217
01:29:21.552 --> 01:29:24.792
Thank you very much.

1218
01:29:25.832 --> 01:29:29.392
Music. One, two, three, four...

1219
01:30:16.992 --> 01:30:19.832
As we wait for the band to tune up,

1220
01:30:19.952 --> 01:30:24.032
it is a great honor for me

1221
01:30:24.152 --> 01:30:28.632
to invite Mr. Jourablou and the groom

1222
01:30:28.752 --> 01:30:30.392
out on the dance floor.

1223
01:30:30.712 --> 01:30:32.032
Are you ready?

1224
01:30:32.952 --> 01:30:34.272
Please.

1225
01:30:34.872 --> 01:30:36.392
I can't hear you!

1226
01:30:38.432 --> 01:30:40.192
Thank you!

1227
01:30:40.552 --> 01:30:44.592
The family patriarch is fabulous!

1228
01:30:44.872 --> 01:30:48.592
The band: One, two, three, four!

1229
01:34:19.112 --> 01:34:20.432
Leila!

1230
01:34:20.912 --> 01:34:22.232
Leila!

1231
01:34:26.512 --> 01:34:29.392
Leila! Leila!

1232
01:34:32.712 --> 01:34:34.032
Leila!

1233
01:34:36.432 --> 01:34:37.752
Leila!

1234
01:34:39.272 --> 01:34:41.592
Stop! Stop!

1235
01:34:44.872 --> 01:34:46.592
Leila, wait!

1236
01:34:50.392 --> 01:34:54.592
Stop! Why are you doing this?
It's a lifetime of disgrace.

1237
01:34:54.712 --> 01:34:56.112
My brothers are unemployed.

1238
01:34:56.232 --> 01:34:58.192
Give me the coins. You're scaring me.

1239
01:34:58.312 --> 01:35:01.392
What're you afraid of?
Your brothers will be overjoyed.

1240
01:35:01.512 --> 01:35:05.712
If they find out what you've done,
they'll kill you.

1241
01:35:05.832 --> 01:35:10.072
- I told you to let Dad come to this wedding.
- He is at the wedding!

1242
01:35:10.192 --> 01:35:11.992
This is worse than if he wasn't.

1243
01:35:12.112 --> 01:35:14.032
I didn't want him to come.

1244
01:35:14.152 --> 01:35:16.552
- It's his money!
- It's his children's due!

1245
01:35:16.672 --> 01:35:19.792
You're wasting your time.
I don't have the coins here!

1246
01:35:19.912 --> 01:35:21.912
Stop being such a chicken.

1247
01:35:22.032 --> 01:35:24.952
Go back, get a grip
and set your brothers up for life.

1248
01:35:25.072 --> 01:35:27.192
I won't go anywhere without the coins.

1249
01:35:27.312 --> 01:35:30.792
Bayram just wants us
to pay for his son's wedding!

1250
01:35:30.912 --> 01:35:34.872
That's what was planned.
It's none of our business.

1251
01:35:34.992 --> 01:35:37.272
It's my business!
I won't give them to you.

1252
01:35:37.392 --> 01:35:39.472
What am I going to say?

1253
01:35:39.592 --> 01:35:43.192
Nothing. Go back, that's all.
They won't have a choice.

1254
01:35:43.312 --> 01:35:46.752
Let's give them the coins
and take them back later.

1255
01:35:46.872 --> 01:35:49.272
- How?
- We'll beg them,

1256
01:35:49.392 --> 01:35:51.992
threaten them, curse them, you name it.

1257
01:35:52.112 --> 01:35:55.272
They fear nothing
because they believe in nothing.

1258
01:35:55.392 --> 01:35:57.792
Go! Don't make it worse
for our brothers.

1259
01:35:57.912 --> 01:36:00.512
You want me to go
watch them be ridiculed?

1260
01:36:00.632 --> 01:36:02.432
Dad is the patriarch now.

1261
01:36:02.552 --> 01:36:04.112
Everyone has to obey him.

1262
01:36:04.232 --> 01:36:08.712
Have him announce
that he's cancelling the gift tradition.

1263
01:36:08.832 --> 01:36:13.152
Dad cares about them more than us.
He would never ruin their wedding.

1264
01:36:13.272 --> 01:36:16.472
Go back,
look Bayram in the eye and tell him

1265
01:36:16.592 --> 01:36:20.112
- to pay for our gift himself.
- What if he refuses?

1266
01:36:20.232 --> 01:36:22.432
He'll be forced to deal with it.

1267
01:36:22.552 --> 01:36:27.192
Don't be afraid. Be firm.
He'll eat out of your hand, you'll see.

1268
01:36:29.512 --> 01:36:31.912
I can't! I'm coming with you.

1269
01:36:32.032 --> 01:36:33.792
Go back!

1270
01:36:57.912 --> 01:37:00.952
Any gift under 500,
round it up with this.

1271
01:37:01.072 --> 01:37:03.192
- And double the coins.
- Yes, sir.

1272
01:37:06.032 --> 01:37:07.792
- How much?
- Half a coin.

1273
01:37:08.832 --> 01:37:11.792
- One coin for Mr. Bapiri.
- Thank you.

1274
01:37:11.912 --> 01:37:14.792
Give 500 to Hassan.

1275
01:37:18.352 --> 01:37:20.592
- How're you?
- Why're you here?

1276
01:37:20.992 --> 01:37:22.312
What's all this?

1277
01:37:22.672 --> 01:37:24.752
Same as for any wedding.

1278
01:37:24.872 --> 01:37:26.392
Meaning?

1279
01:37:27.272 --> 01:37:30.592
We inflate the smaller gifts to create hype.

1280
01:37:30.912 --> 01:37:33.472
We need you to do it for us, as well.

1281
01:37:33.592 --> 01:37:36.032
- You're kidding?
- I'm not.

1282
01:37:36.152 --> 01:37:38.392
Step out so we can talk.

1283
01:37:51.472 --> 01:37:52.792
What's going on?

1284
01:37:53.072 --> 01:37:54.992
You need to help us out.

1285
01:37:55.192 --> 01:37:57.472
We invited you to help us out.

1286
01:37:57.592 --> 01:37:59.072
- We don't have the coins.
- What?

1287
01:37:59.192 --> 01:38:00.792
We need coins.

1288
01:38:01.272 --> 01:38:04.032
- You're kidding me?
- You give them coins.

1289
01:38:04.152 --> 01:38:08.352
Not at all.
They give them back in the other room.

1290
01:38:08.472 --> 01:38:10.392
Over here. I can't hear you.

1291
01:38:15.512 --> 01:38:17.672
- Tell me.
- We don't have them.

1292
01:38:17.792 --> 01:38:19.432
I just talked to your dad.

1293
01:38:19.552 --> 01:38:21.592
- And?
- He said you had 40 coins.

1294
01:38:21.712 --> 01:38:23.552
I swear I don't have a cent.

1295
01:38:23.672 --> 01:38:25.672
This is not the time. Let me count.

1296
01:38:25.792 --> 01:38:27.552
I swear there are no coins.

1297
01:38:27.672 --> 01:38:30.552
I insisted your dad accept
only if he could afford it.

1298
01:38:30.672 --> 01:38:32.392
I didn't force him.

1299
01:38:32.512 --> 01:38:34.992
No, you melted his heart.

1300
01:38:38.752 --> 01:38:41.592
Give me 35.
I'll have them announce 40.

1301
01:38:41.712 --> 01:38:44.992
Do us a favor,
give the entire amount in our name.

1302
01:38:45.112 --> 01:38:48.552
- Let me talk to him.
- My dad can't find out. Help us.

1303
01:38:48.672 --> 01:38:52.792
What about my reputation?
Your gift was paying for the venue.

1304
01:38:52.912 --> 01:38:55.032
You could've gone elsewhere.

1305
01:38:55.152 --> 01:38:57.792
And marry my only son
in a parking lot like you?

1306
01:38:57.912 --> 01:38:59.592
What do you want to do?

1307
01:38:59.832 --> 01:39:02.992
That's the way things stand.
There's no turning back.

1308
01:39:03.112 --> 01:39:05.792
You idiot, there's no turning back for you.

1309
01:39:05.912 --> 01:39:09.072
You're marrying your son,
and my dad is the patriarch.

1310
01:39:09.192 --> 01:39:11.552
Ghardashali is here with 50 coins.

1311
01:39:11.672 --> 01:39:13.352
In his pocket?

1312
01:39:13.472 --> 01:39:15.552
In his check book.
Know what that is?

1313
01:39:15.672 --> 01:39:17.192
Ghardashali's pathetic.

1314
01:39:17.312 --> 01:39:20.312
Less than you.
He's not ruining the wedding.

1315
01:39:20.432 --> 01:39:22.352
My father is the patriarch.

1316
01:39:22.472 --> 01:39:26.472
I can have him cancel the wedding gifts.

1317
01:39:26.592 --> 01:39:29.592
Are you threatening me?

1318
01:39:29.752 --> 01:39:31.072
Suppose I am.

1319
01:39:33.632 --> 01:39:37.432
When your father accepted,
he signed a contract

1320
01:39:37.552 --> 01:39:39.112
saying he'd give 40 coins.

1321
01:39:39.232 --> 01:39:43.592
I'll do you the favor
of not pressing charges.

1322
01:39:43.712 --> 01:39:48.352
Now, keep a low profile,
eat your dinner and go back to your hovel.

1323
01:39:48.472 --> 01:39:51.392
He's 80 and sick.
You can't do this to him.

1324
01:39:51.512 --> 01:39:53.952
You whining little shit,

1325
01:39:54.072 --> 01:39:57.672
threatening me when you think you can,
begging when you can't!

1326
01:39:57.792 --> 01:40:00.192
Everything they say about you people is true.

1327
01:40:00.312 --> 01:40:03.552
You're a bunch of lazy, retarded bums!

1328
01:40:03.672 --> 01:40:06.152
Don't ruin your son's wedding.

1329
01:40:06.272 --> 01:40:08.792
Who wants to ruin my son's wedding?

1330
01:40:08.912 --> 01:40:10.392
Esmail-the-beggar's son?

1331
01:40:13.912 --> 01:40:17.632
My brothers won't listen to you like I have.

1332
01:40:17.752 --> 01:40:20.632
Go tell your brothers to spoil the party.

1333
01:40:20.752 --> 01:40:22.072
Do it!

1334
01:40:23.312 --> 01:40:27.312
Cousin, I've been begging you for an hour.

1335
01:40:27.432 --> 01:40:30.552
Shut your mouth.
Go tell them to ruin the party.

1336
01:40:30.672 --> 01:40:32.952
Who were you counting on to spoil it?

1337
01:40:33.072 --> 01:40:35.992
Your degenerate brothers
or your imbecile father?

1338
01:40:36.752 --> 01:40:42.112
I can tie both my legs and an arm
and still beat the four of you.

1339
01:40:42.232 --> 01:40:44.952
Want me to kick your father off that stage,

1340
01:40:45.072 --> 01:40:49.832
make you get on all fours
and sit Ghardashali on your backs?

1341
01:40:49.952 --> 01:40:51.272
Want that?

1342
01:40:54.392 --> 01:40:57.992
If any of you bat an eyelid tonight,

1343
01:40:58.112 --> 01:41:04.392
I'll make mincemeat of you all
and feed you to my son for his wedding.

1344
01:41:29.872 --> 01:41:31.992
DJ! Switch it off!

1345
01:43:15.952 --> 01:43:17.512
The time has come

1346
01:43:17.632 --> 01:43:21.192
to present the gifts,
but with a minor change.

1347
01:43:22.192 --> 01:43:28.392
Luckily, nowadays,
we can talk our differences through.

1348
01:43:28.792 --> 01:43:35.192
Tonight, at the request of our patriarch,
Mr. Esmail Jourablou,

1349
01:43:35.352 --> 01:43:39.592
the first gift will be presented
by Mr. Ghardashali Jourablou.

1350
01:43:40.752 --> 01:43:46.792
Esmail, our guest of honor,
will keep us company with his sons.

1351
01:43:47.072 --> 01:43:48.392
And now...

1352
01:43:48.552 --> 01:43:49.872
let me present,

1353
01:43:50.832 --> 01:43:54.792
on this day, at this hour,
in this glorious second,

1354
01:43:55.072 --> 01:43:56.792
the family patriarch

1355
01:43:57.112 --> 01:44:00.272
and successor to the late Gholam Jourablou,

1356
01:44:00.392 --> 01:44:06.192
Mr. Ghardashali Jourablou!

1357
01:44:58.592 --> 01:45:03.392
I congratulate you
for all the applause and energy.

1358
01:45:05.792 --> 01:45:08.192
The first gift,

1359
01:45:08.312 --> 01:45:09.872
offered by the family patriarch,

1360
01:45:09.992 --> 01:45:13.792
Mr. Ghardashali Jourablou.

1361
01:45:13.912 --> 01:45:15.912
70 million tomans.

1362
01:45:16.032 --> 01:45:19.672
The equivalent of 50 gold coins.

1363
01:45:19.792 --> 01:45:22.792
Blessed he be!

1364
01:45:22.952 --> 01:45:24.272
Thank you!

1365
01:45:28.072 --> 01:45:29.592
Well done!

1366
01:46:00.792 --> 01:46:03.672
Why are you locking the door?
Wait, Esmail.

1367
01:46:03.792 --> 01:46:07.512
Don't lock the door.
Come back, please.

1368
01:46:07.632 --> 01:46:12.912
I'll make you some nice tea.
Take your opium, you'll feel better.

1369
01:46:13.032 --> 01:46:14.352
Come here.

1370
01:46:20.752 --> 01:46:24.272
In two days, the price of coins
has gone up by 200,000.

1371
01:46:24.392 --> 01:46:26.392
- How much did you sell them?
- 1.4 million.

1372
01:46:26.512 --> 01:46:29.592
- What time do we get up?
- Leila, wake me up at 7.

1373
01:46:29.952 --> 01:46:32.872
You were all in on it?

1374
01:46:32.992 --> 01:46:36.792
Manouchehr's sleeping here
because he sold his apartment.

1375
01:46:37.672 --> 01:46:41.512
Farhad sold his car,
and is picking up the money at 8 a.m.

1376
01:46:41.632 --> 01:46:43.912
At 10, we're signing for the shop.

1377
01:46:44.032 --> 01:46:47.312
Without telling me?
Why'd you drag me into this?

1378
01:46:47.432 --> 01:46:50.192
Without you, it wouldn't have worked.

1379
01:46:50.312 --> 01:46:54.032
- But you did it all yourselves.
- With your help.

1380
01:46:54.152 --> 01:46:55.872
I got played.

1381
01:46:55.992 --> 01:46:59.752
If I'd had a say,
you wouldn't have bought the shop.

1382
01:46:59.872 --> 01:47:02.152
Alireza, you handled it perfectly.

1383
01:47:02.272 --> 01:47:05.592
Hats off to you.
I would've had a heart attack. Right?

1384
01:47:05.712 --> 01:47:08.752
- Yup.
- Why didn't you say anything?

1385
01:47:08.872 --> 01:47:12.192
We did and you refused.
We didn't insist.

1386
01:47:12.312 --> 01:47:15.792
What's troubling you?
You did a good job.

1387
01:47:15.912 --> 01:47:17.232
What job?

1388
01:47:17.432 --> 01:47:19.272
You think I'm an idiot?

1389
01:47:19.392 --> 01:47:22.752
He's right.
You weren't supposed to be in on it.

1390
01:47:22.872 --> 01:47:26.192
We did the thinking, you performed.
And you did good.

1391
01:47:26.312 --> 01:47:28.392
You were thinking for me?

1392
01:47:28.832 --> 01:47:33.152
You should tell us whose name
goes on the paperwork tomorrow.

1393
01:47:33.272 --> 01:47:35.992
The deed will be issued in that name.

1394
01:47:36.112 --> 01:47:39.592
Dad's, of course,
so we can look him in the eye again.

1395
01:47:39.712 --> 01:47:41.832
So he can sell the shop out of spite?

1396
01:47:41.952 --> 01:47:43.752
Or give it to Bayram.

1397
01:47:43.872 --> 01:47:45.592
Leila signs.

1398
01:47:45.912 --> 01:47:47.312
"Leila & Bros." sounds nice.

1399
01:47:47.432 --> 01:47:51.232
It's not my shop.
One of you has to sign.

1400
01:47:51.352 --> 01:47:53.352
- Like who?
- Take a vote.

1401
01:47:53.472 --> 01:47:56.592
Farhad thinks with his pecs,

1402
01:47:56.912 --> 01:47:58.232
so not him.

1403
01:47:58.832 --> 01:48:03.832
Parviz is overweight
and might have a heart attack any time.

1404
01:48:03.952 --> 01:48:05.952
- Not him either.
- And you're a thief.

1405
01:48:06.072 --> 01:48:07.392
You'll end up in jail.

1406
01:48:07.512 --> 01:48:10.392
- So not me.
- That leaves Alireza.

1407
01:48:10.512 --> 01:48:13.192
- I vote for Alireza.
- Logical.

1408
01:48:14.232 --> 01:48:16.712
- Leila?
- I abstain.

1409
01:48:16.832 --> 01:48:18.592
- Who do you vote for?
- I'm not saying.

1410
01:48:18.712 --> 01:48:20.152
- You have to.
- And you?

1411
01:48:20.272 --> 01:48:23.072
I won't vote.
But you're not voting for me, right?

1412
01:48:23.192 --> 01:48:24.512
Not anymore.

1413
01:48:24.712 --> 01:48:26.792
Why not? Why?

1414
01:48:27.432 --> 01:48:30.552
'Cause you're a coward.
That's why you're shouting.

1415
01:48:30.672 --> 01:48:33.232
We spare you and you get excited.

1416
01:48:33.352 --> 01:48:37.592
I made you stay
to save you from your shitty lives.

1417
01:48:37.752 --> 01:48:39.472
But you just don't see it.

1418
01:48:39.592 --> 01:48:43.392
Who got us into deep shit tonight?

1419
01:48:43.512 --> 01:48:46.432
How dare you defend your asshole father.

1420
01:48:46.552 --> 01:48:49.152
Have you no shame?

1421
01:48:49.272 --> 01:48:52.672
You humiliated that poor,
naive, old man so badly,

1422
01:48:52.792 --> 01:48:56.592
till his death he won't forget
what he went through tonight.

1423
01:48:56.832 --> 01:48:59.032
All you see is him?
What about them?

1424
01:48:59.152 --> 01:49:03.912
Because of you
there's no affection left between them.

1425
01:49:04.032 --> 01:49:06.192
They're forced to live together.

1426
01:49:06.312 --> 01:49:07.632
That's not my doing.

1427
01:49:07.752 --> 01:49:11.192
They're here.
They know the parents better than you do.

1428
01:49:11.552 --> 01:49:15.792
They don't show up every 8 years
in a hurry to leave again.

1429
01:49:15.912 --> 01:49:18.592
Mom and Dad may be senile now,

1430
01:49:18.912 --> 01:49:21.192
but tonight, I saw it with my own eyes.

1431
01:49:21.472 --> 01:49:25.392
I saw that you're behind
everyone's misfortune here.

1432
01:49:56.112 --> 01:49:59.392
Sign all three pages of this copy, as well.

1433
01:50:06.312 --> 01:50:07.752
Congratulations.

1434
01:50:07.872 --> 01:50:09.232
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

1435
01:50:09.352 --> 01:50:12.512
Thank you for everything.

1436
01:50:12.632 --> 01:50:14.192
This is your copy.

1437
01:50:14.712 --> 01:50:17.592
- Mr. Property Owner!
- Alireza...

1438
01:50:18.112 --> 01:50:21.592
- Thank you, sir.
- Can you hand me an envelope?

1439
01:50:23.832 --> 01:50:27.792
- Here you go. Congratulations.
- Congratulations to you!

1440
01:50:27.912 --> 01:50:29.392
See you tonight.

1441
01:50:40.072 --> 01:50:41.392
'Evening.

1442
01:50:45.672 --> 01:50:46.992
Already here?

1443
01:50:47.872 --> 01:50:49.992
You should've waited a few days.

1444
01:50:57.432 --> 01:50:59.192
He hasn't come out yet?

1445
01:51:00.672 --> 01:51:01.992
Dad?

1446
01:51:02.392 --> 01:51:04.752
Mom says he hasn't eaten
or taken his pills.

1447
01:51:04.872 --> 01:51:06.392
Hasn't even gone to the bathroom.

1448
01:51:07.952 --> 01:51:09.472
Maybe something's happened?

1449
01:51:09.592 --> 01:51:11.392
No, I can hear his lighter.

1450
01:51:12.032 --> 01:51:13.952
Thank you for this, Ali.

1451
01:51:14.072 --> 01:51:16.232
Don't make things worse, Mom.

1452
01:51:16.352 --> 01:51:20.552
- Dad...
- What you did to your father last night,

1453
01:51:20.672 --> 01:51:23.272
no one would do to their worst enemy.

1454
01:51:23.392 --> 01:51:27.392
Soon, you won't know
how to thank us for last night.

1455
01:51:27.552 --> 01:51:29.192
We didn't do anything wrong.

1456
01:51:29.312 --> 01:51:32.992
We bought a shop
in one of the best malls of Tehran.

1457
01:51:33.552 --> 01:51:36.512
Dad, it's the mall where I work.

1458
01:51:36.632 --> 01:51:38.152
It's legit.

1459
01:51:38.272 --> 01:51:43.992
We didn't buy it just with your coins.
We pitched in everything we had.

1460
01:51:44.312 --> 01:51:47.432
Come see it tomorrow.
If you don't like it...

1461
01:51:47.552 --> 01:51:50.192
Stop talking nonsense.

1462
01:51:50.312 --> 01:51:52.792
Whatever next? Go back inside.

1463
01:51:53.032 --> 01:51:55.392
Parviz, he's fine. Go inside.

1464
01:52:03.432 --> 01:52:05.392
Dad, don't listen to them.

1465
01:52:05.592 --> 01:52:08.792
I'm the one who signed.
I have the deed.

1466
01:52:09.112 --> 01:52:13.792
Let's go tomorrow.
If you like it, it's yours.

1467
01:52:14.592 --> 01:52:19.392
And if you don't like it,
I swear I'll cancel the sale.

1468
01:52:19.632 --> 01:52:21.992
I'll buy back your coins
and give them to you.

1469
01:52:23.192 --> 01:52:25.592
But first, come see the place.

1470
01:52:28.472 --> 01:52:29.792
Dad?

1471
01:52:41.312 --> 01:52:42.632
This way, Dad.

1472
01:52:43.352 --> 01:52:44.992
Our shop will be here.

1473
01:52:46.672 --> 01:52:47.992
Right here.

1474
01:52:49.912 --> 01:52:51.232
Look.

1475
01:52:52.352 --> 01:52:53.672
This is it.

1476
01:53:05.072 --> 01:53:07.392
Wait, Dad. Let me explain.

1477
01:53:07.752 --> 01:53:11.392
Buying this shop
is a very good decision.

1478
01:53:12.032 --> 01:53:14.352
I'm telling you this,

1479
01:53:14.472 --> 01:53:19.192
and I swear I wasn't in the know
at the wedding.

1480
01:53:19.752 --> 01:53:22.232
Business is so good here,

1481
01:53:22.352 --> 01:53:25.592
that they're replacing the toilets
with eight shops.

1482
01:53:25.752 --> 01:53:27.952
We'll have the best one.

1483
01:53:28.072 --> 01:53:32.592
Our shop will be 6.5 by 10 feet.
The shopfront will be 10 feet wide.

1484
01:53:33.032 --> 01:53:36.432
It'll start exactly here.

1485
01:53:36.552 --> 01:53:40.392
One, two, three...
All the way to the back.

1486
01:53:40.632 --> 01:53:41.952
All that...

1487
01:53:42.592 --> 01:53:43.912
Sorry.

1488
01:53:45.152 --> 01:53:50.072
And in this direction,
6.5 feet to the hallway we came in from.

1489
01:53:50.192 --> 01:53:54.032
- You saw it.
- Next to a couple of the best shops.

1490
01:53:54.152 --> 01:53:55.592
It's an excellent location.

1491
01:53:55.872 --> 01:53:57.592
It's a popular spot.

1492
01:53:57.712 --> 01:54:01.992
They gave it to us
because Leila and Parviz work here.

1493
01:54:02.312 --> 01:54:06.472
Dad, try to forget what you're hearing
and seeing here today.

1494
01:54:06.592 --> 01:54:09.832
In three months, you'll love it.

1495
01:54:09.952 --> 01:54:13.792
Come spend a day with me, you'll see.

1496
01:54:13.952 --> 01:54:18.072
Dad... The four of us will work hard.

1497
01:54:18.192 --> 01:54:19.992
We're gonna make a buck.

1498
01:54:21.432 --> 01:54:23.192
Much good may it do you.

1499
01:54:24.152 --> 01:54:25.672
I'll see you in court.

1500
01:54:25.792 --> 01:54:28.312
- Dad...
- Why in court, Dad?

1501
01:54:28.432 --> 01:54:31.912
Think of it as a buildable lot.

1502
01:54:32.032 --> 01:54:35.192
Don't you trust my economic instinct?

1503
01:54:35.312 --> 01:54:38.472
Didn't you save those coins
for your kids' future?

1504
01:54:38.592 --> 01:54:41.792
- The future is now.
- I don't want kids like you.

1505
01:54:42.152 --> 01:54:44.872
Alireza, I trusted you.

1506
01:54:44.992 --> 01:54:47.192
It was the worst mistake of my life.

1507
01:54:48.632 --> 01:54:52.592
You removed my crown
to buy bathroom stalls?

1508
01:54:52.912 --> 01:54:55.752
Give me my coins back right now!

1509
01:54:55.872 --> 01:54:58.192
Leila works here.
This is awkward. Listen...

1510
01:54:58.312 --> 01:55:01.432
I won't listen! I mortgaged the house.

1511
01:55:01.552 --> 01:55:04.032
If I don't return them,
you'll all be homeless.

1512
01:55:04.152 --> 01:55:05.472
A mortgage?

1513
01:55:05.912 --> 01:55:08.792
I got a mortgage to buy the coins.

1514
01:55:08.992 --> 01:55:10.632
You're humiliating me again.

1515
01:55:10.752 --> 01:55:12.912
You shouldn't have had kids!

1516
01:55:13.032 --> 01:55:15.952
And stop shouting, you old fool.
People are staring!

1517
01:55:16.072 --> 01:55:17.392
Shut up!

1518
01:55:17.952 --> 01:55:19.992
- I had you...
- Cool it.

1519
01:55:20.752 --> 01:55:23.392
I fed and raised you.

1520
01:55:23.512 --> 01:55:25.792
Now go fuck yourselves!

1521
01:55:26.392 --> 01:55:29.472
Why should I support you in your forties?

1522
01:55:29.592 --> 01:55:32.792
- Why?
- Calm down.

1523
01:55:33.712 --> 01:55:35.032
My gold coins.

1524
01:55:35.632 --> 01:55:36.952
Okay!

1525
01:55:37.752 --> 01:55:39.912
He's going to pass out.

1526
01:55:40.032 --> 01:55:42.592
- Dad!
- He's passing out!

1527
01:55:42.912 --> 01:55:45.392
Call an ambulance!

1528
01:55:46.192 --> 01:55:47.792
Dad, I'm sorry.

1529
01:55:49.792 --> 01:55:51.512
We need sugar.

1530
01:55:52.112 --> 01:55:53.952
Call an ambulance.

1531
01:55:54.232 --> 01:55:55.552
Some water, please.

1532
01:55:59.152 --> 01:56:00.472
- Dad!
- Dad!

1533
01:56:00.592 --> 01:56:01.912
Dad!

1534
01:56:02.112 --> 01:56:04.672
- Dad! Dad!
- Dad!

1535
01:56:04.832 --> 01:56:06.352
- Dad!
- Dad!

1536
01:56:06.952 --> 01:56:10.792
- Talk!
- Gimme that!

1537
01:56:18.032 --> 01:56:19.352
I'm exhausted.

1538
01:56:21.232 --> 01:56:23.112
I can't do this anymore.

1539
01:56:23.232 --> 01:56:26.392
I can't...

1540
01:56:27.152 --> 01:56:29.192
Prices are rocketing.

1541
01:56:29.752 --> 01:56:32.392
It could even get worse than this.

1542
01:56:33.152 --> 01:56:35.232
Then before it gets out of hand,

1543
01:56:35.352 --> 01:56:38.592
we should return the shop
and buy his coins back.

1544
01:56:41.992 --> 01:56:44.392
You'll have to kill me

1545
01:56:44.992 --> 01:56:46.592
to return that shop.

1546
01:56:49.472 --> 01:56:52.392
Do you know why he's panicking like this?

1547
01:56:52.592 --> 01:56:56.392
He put a mortgage on the house
to buy the coins.

1548
01:57:00.672 --> 01:57:03.192
- Says who?
- Him.

1549
01:57:04.952 --> 01:57:07.392
- He couldn't.
- He did.

1550
01:57:08.112 --> 01:57:10.792
If he hadn't, he wouldn't be here.

1551
01:57:34.912 --> 01:57:37.992
Leila didn't see the scene
he made at the mall.

1552
01:57:38.112 --> 01:57:41.392
It was payback for being dethroned.

1553
01:57:41.512 --> 01:57:43.712
Payback? He's the one in the hospital.

1554
01:57:43.832 --> 01:57:47.232
Leila's plan aside,

1555
01:57:47.352 --> 01:57:50.632
I never would've thought
Bayram would do this to Dad.

1556
01:57:50.752 --> 01:57:53.112
Me neither. It's hard to believe.

1557
01:57:53.232 --> 01:57:56.072
Leila couldn't have guessed he'd go so far.

1558
01:57:56.192 --> 01:57:59.712
You think if Leila had known
Bayram would kick Dad off stage,

1559
01:57:59.832 --> 01:58:01.592
she wouldn't have taken the coins?

1560
01:58:02.752 --> 01:58:05.392
We return them or we lose the house.

1561
01:58:05.512 --> 01:58:07.992
We'll return them, of course.

1562
01:58:08.472 --> 01:58:11.392
- Thanks to the shop.
- We're going to lose him.

1563
01:58:12.432 --> 01:58:15.992
If anything happens to him,
you won't see me again.

1564
01:58:17.072 --> 01:58:18.392
Too bad.

1565
01:58:20.192 --> 01:58:24.192
You think he'll surrender?
He'll resist until it kills him.

1566
01:58:24.872 --> 01:58:26.192
Let him die.

1567
01:58:29.272 --> 01:58:32.912
For once in his life,
he found money at the right time.

1568
01:58:33.032 --> 01:58:38.512
And instead of letting Bayram extort him,
we put it to good use.

1569
01:58:38.632 --> 01:58:41.352
You call your dirty tricks good use?

1570
01:58:41.472 --> 01:58:44.392
- Pretend we got a loan.
- He's going to die.

1571
01:58:45.232 --> 01:58:46.592
He lost face.

1572
01:58:46.752 --> 01:58:49.272
His house is at stake.
He can't breathe.

1573
01:58:49.392 --> 01:58:50.992
Imagine he'd given it to Bayram.

1574
01:58:51.112 --> 01:58:53.152
He wouldn't be in intensive care.

1575
01:58:53.272 --> 01:58:55.392
And we wouldn't have a shop.

1576
01:58:55.512 --> 01:58:57.992
Dad cursed that shop.

1577
01:58:58.112 --> 01:59:00.672
It'll never turn a profit.

1578
01:59:00.792 --> 01:59:04.632
- Parviz?
- I've been this guy's son for 50 years.

1579
01:59:04.752 --> 01:59:06.192
Half a century.

1580
01:59:06.592 --> 01:59:08.952
When he digs in his heels,

1581
01:59:09.072 --> 01:59:11.952
he goes all the way.

1582
01:59:12.072 --> 01:59:13.712
Alireza's right.

1583
01:59:13.832 --> 01:59:17.232
He won't let up until he drops dead.

1584
01:59:17.352 --> 01:59:22.792
By the time the shop's up and running,
we'll have lost our house and everything.

1585
01:59:23.472 --> 01:59:26.392
At what cost will we start a business?

1586
01:59:26.552 --> 01:59:29.552
There's a huge waiting list for that shop.

1587
01:59:29.672 --> 01:59:32.032
At what cost will we lose this opportunity?

1588
01:59:32.152 --> 01:59:34.192
At the cost of our roof.

1589
01:59:35.992 --> 01:59:41.792
At the cost of our father's life.
But to you, that's worth nothing.

1590
01:59:43.432 --> 01:59:44.752
Manouchehr.

1591
01:59:48.672 --> 01:59:52.192
- Nothing to add?
- Nothing you'll like hearing.

1592
01:59:54.112 --> 01:59:55.792
Doesn't matter. Say it anyway.

1593
01:59:56.072 --> 01:59:59.952
For the shop to turn a profit,
we'll need time and capital.

1594
02:00:00.072 --> 02:00:03.192
- We have neither.
- That shop is a good investment,

1595
02:00:03.312 --> 02:00:05.592
even if it stays closed.

1596
02:00:05.752 --> 02:00:09.992
Even if we were to lose the house,
which we won't.

1597
02:00:11.112 --> 02:00:14.832
If he'd given the coins to Bayram,
how would he have returned them?

1598
02:00:14.952 --> 02:00:16.272
We'll do the same.

1599
02:00:17.752 --> 02:00:24.432
He didn't think about how he'd pay them back.
He just wanted to be up on that stage.

1600
02:00:24.552 --> 02:00:27.072
We're capable of anything in this family.

1601
02:00:27.192 --> 02:00:29.752
If we lose the house, we'll be homeless.

1602
02:00:29.872 --> 02:00:32.632
The potential of that shop is beyond compare.

1603
02:00:32.752 --> 02:00:35.472
With it, all of you will become homeowners.

1604
02:00:35.592 --> 02:00:37.392
We're doing this for us.

1605
02:00:37.632 --> 02:00:39.592
We also invested our money.

1606
02:00:39.792 --> 02:00:42.192
So our opinion should count, too.

1607
02:00:42.632 --> 02:00:44.992
- Let's take a vote.
- A vote?

1608
02:00:48.592 --> 02:00:49.912
Alireza...

1609
02:00:50.712 --> 02:00:54.392
have you brainwashed them
into returning the shop?

1610
02:00:56.832 --> 02:01:00.192
Will you accept the consequences
or share the blame?

1611
02:01:21.272 --> 02:01:23.992
You'll remember this night
for the rest of your lives.

1612
02:01:26.872 --> 02:01:32.192
You'll regret making this absurd decision
and not listening to me.

1613
02:01:32.752 --> 02:01:36.592
You are ruining the biggest opportunity
of your lives.

1614
02:01:37.392 --> 02:01:41.192
You're sentencing yourselves
to eternal poverty, here and now.

1615
02:02:25.632 --> 02:02:26.952
Are you sure?

1616
02:02:29.952 --> 02:02:31.272
Cancel it.

1617
02:02:43.592 --> 02:02:44.912
Hello.

1618
02:02:45.272 --> 02:02:48.112
- I'd like 40 gold coins.
- 2.5 million each.

1619
02:02:48.232 --> 02:02:51.592
You mean 1.5 million?
We just sold them for 1.4.

1620
02:02:51.712 --> 02:02:55.392
- No, man. It's 2.5 now.
- But why?

1621
02:02:55.512 --> 02:02:59.032
The US wants to abandon
the nuclear deal. Excuse me.

1622
02:02:59.152 --> 02:03:01.392
They want to. They haven't yet.

1623
02:03:01.512 --> 02:03:03.912
- We'll see.
- Can you buzz us out?

1624
02:03:04.032 --> 02:03:05.352
They won't do it.

1625
02:03:05.592 --> 02:03:07.992
- Hello.
- Hello.

1626
02:03:08.152 --> 02:03:09.472
We want 40 coins.

1627
02:03:09.592 --> 02:03:12.792
3 million each. That makes 120 million.

1628
02:03:13.512 --> 02:03:16.472
It was 100 million across the street.
2.5 each.

1629
02:03:16.592 --> 02:03:20.792
- Tomorrow, it'll be 150.
- Can I ask you a question?

1630
02:03:20.952 --> 02:03:23.272
For 40 coins, should we wait or buy?

1631
02:03:23.392 --> 02:03:26.992
- Wait. Prices might come down.
- Will they?

1632
02:03:29.672 --> 02:03:31.792
We came earlier.

1633
02:03:32.152 --> 02:03:34.672
For 40 coins can you give us a discount?

1634
02:03:34.792 --> 02:03:37.592
The site was just updated.
It's now 3 million.

1635
02:03:39.872 --> 02:03:41.992
But we were just here.

1636
02:03:42.192 --> 02:03:43.512
What can I say?

1637
02:03:51.312 --> 02:03:55.472
Right now, on line,
40 coins are going for 200 million.

1638
02:03:55.592 --> 02:03:58.192
- Before it was 100 million.
- Before...

1639
02:03:58.312 --> 02:03:59.752
We don't know what's going on.

1640
02:03:59.872 --> 02:04:02.712
It's nuts. 5 million per coin?

1641
02:04:02.872 --> 02:04:04.392
No way, it's a bubble.

1642
02:04:04.512 --> 02:04:06.432
Next week it should go back down to 1.

1643
02:04:06.552 --> 02:04:09.192
See, even he says so.

1644
02:04:11.272 --> 02:04:12.592
Thanks.

1645
02:04:17.992 --> 02:04:21.392
- What do we do, Manouchehr?
- We buy before it goes higher.

1646
02:04:21.552 --> 02:04:24.592
If no one buys,
they'll have to bring prices down.

1647
02:04:24.992 --> 02:04:27.712
- The bubble will pop.
- Mr. Economist,

1648
02:04:27.832 --> 02:04:30.352
it's a stainless-steel bubble.
It won't pop.

1649
02:04:30.472 --> 02:04:33.872
Taxi driver analysis.
I say we don't buy.

1650
02:04:33.992 --> 02:04:35.312
It's up to you.

1651
02:04:35.512 --> 02:04:38.792
How many can you buy
with all the money?

1652
02:04:39.392 --> 02:04:41.992
- About 30.
- Buy them, then.

1653
02:04:42.712 --> 02:04:44.592
Manouchehr says it'll come back down.

1654
02:04:45.152 --> 02:04:50.392
I've lived in this country for 70 years,
I've never seen prices come down.

1655
02:04:50.872 --> 02:04:52.792
They have to want them to.

1656
02:04:53.112 --> 02:04:55.432
May God help my children.

1657
02:04:55.552 --> 02:04:59.192
I'm afraid if we buy at 5 mil,
the next day it'll go down to 1.

1658
02:05:05.352 --> 02:05:07.192
Thank you sir, bye.

1659
02:05:08.592 --> 02:05:11.192
Hello, sir.

1660
02:05:12.112 --> 02:05:14.032
- We want some gold coins.
- How many?

1661
02:05:14.152 --> 02:05:15.472
40.

1662
02:05:18.512 --> 02:05:19.832
320 million.

1663
02:05:21.392 --> 02:05:23.792
One gold coin costs 8 million?

1664
02:05:23.912 --> 02:05:27.352
The dollar just went
from 3,000 to 19,000. It's normal.

1665
02:05:27.472 --> 02:05:29.632
You agree that it's a bubble?

1666
02:05:29.752 --> 02:05:32.272
The dollar's set
to cross the 30,000 mark.

1667
02:05:32.392 --> 02:05:35.272
Yesterday, a coin cost 6.
After Trump's speech,

1668
02:05:35.392 --> 02:05:37.592
it went up to 7. After his tweet, 8.

1669
02:05:43.472 --> 02:05:46.392
- Thank you, sir.
- You're welcome. Have a nice day.

1670
02:05:46.992 --> 02:05:49.192
Is a tweet a bomb?

1671
02:05:49.352 --> 02:05:51.632
No, but even a bomb shouldn't do this.

1672
02:05:51.752 --> 02:05:53.072
Let's go, Dad.

1673
02:07:37.072 --> 02:07:39.192
A gold coin now costs 14 million.

1674
02:07:39.752 --> 02:07:41.592
The US dollar is at 28,000.

1675
02:07:41.832 --> 02:07:46.992
- Stop it, that's enough.
- Damn whoever's responsible for this.

1676
02:07:48.112 --> 02:07:50.792
You sold the car 19 million, Farhad?

1677
02:07:51.072 --> 02:07:53.992
- Yes.
- Now it's worth 100 million.

1678
02:07:54.672 --> 02:07:56.792
Still think it's a bubble?

1679
02:07:58.152 --> 02:08:00.192
If you had that shop,

1680
02:08:00.552 --> 02:08:03.192
it would be worth
at least six times as much now.

1681
02:08:03.752 --> 02:08:06.192
If that's the case, go get it back.

1682
02:08:09.552 --> 02:08:10.872
What did you say, Dad?

1683
02:08:11.632 --> 02:08:13.192
They'll never agree.

1684
02:08:13.672 --> 02:08:15.792
No harm in asking.

1685
02:08:29.272 --> 02:08:31.392
The US dollar crossed the 30,000 mark.

1686
02:08:34.912 --> 02:08:37.192
We can return three of Dad's coins.

1687
02:08:37.352 --> 02:08:38.992
Is that supposed to be funny?

1688
02:08:39.992 --> 02:08:41.392
You don't give a shit.

1689
02:08:47.312 --> 02:08:48.632
Check out the car.

1690
02:08:54.192 --> 02:08:56.392
That's not a car, it's a tank.

1691
02:09:44.392 --> 02:09:47.992
You'll get a stiff neck! They're gone.

1692
02:09:51.472 --> 02:09:56.152
If we'd taken over your friend's office,
we'd each have one of those cars.

1693
02:09:56.272 --> 02:09:57.792
And one of those girls.

1694
02:09:57.912 --> 02:10:00.792
All that fat is interfering with your brain.

1695
02:10:00.912 --> 02:10:05.792
If we'd taken over,
we'd owe a thousand times 120 mil!

1696
02:10:05.912 --> 02:10:07.392
I think just the opposite.

1697
02:10:07.512 --> 02:10:10.192
That's all you do, think the opposite.

1698
02:10:10.432 --> 02:10:14.792
Prides were going for 20 million,
now they're 116.

1699
02:10:15.352 --> 02:10:18.192
I presold 915 Prides.

1700
02:10:18.592 --> 02:10:22.232
Know what 915 times 116 million comes to?

1701
02:10:22.672 --> 02:10:25.592
106 billion 140 million tomans!

1702
02:10:25.712 --> 02:10:28.792
And not one customer
accepts their original 20.

1703
02:10:29.152 --> 02:10:33.592
We had two months to deliver.
I have ten days left.

1704
02:10:33.832 --> 02:10:35.632
I have 10 days

1705
02:10:35.752 --> 02:10:37.832
to either deliver 915 cars

1706
02:10:37.952 --> 02:10:40.912
or come up
with 106 billion and 140 million.

1707
02:10:41.032 --> 02:10:44.992
If prices stop going up.

1708
02:10:48.832 --> 02:10:50.152
Well done.

1709
02:11:00.512 --> 02:11:01.992
So what do we do?

1710
02:11:02.112 --> 02:11:04.592
My calculations were perfect.

1711
02:11:05.072 --> 02:11:10.752
- If prices hadn't shot up, we'd be rich.
- What's the solution now?

1712
02:11:10.872 --> 02:11:12.952
I say we sue the guy.

1713
02:11:13.072 --> 02:11:15.592
I signed a contract. What do you think?

1714
02:11:15.712 --> 02:11:18.752
Then turn yourself in and settle this.

1715
02:11:18.872 --> 02:11:20.392
What if I can't settle it?

1716
02:11:20.992 --> 02:11:22.672
What if I get 20 years?

1717
02:11:22.792 --> 02:11:24.832
Is your roommate at that office?

1718
02:11:24.952 --> 02:11:27.112
No, I'm managing it.

1719
02:11:27.232 --> 02:11:29.392
- Where is he now?
- I don't know.

1720
02:11:29.792 --> 02:11:31.112
He's gone.

1721
02:11:31.512 --> 02:11:34.792
I looked for him.
He's nowhere to be found.

1722
02:11:42.872 --> 02:11:46.392
Then you have to leave the country.

1723
02:11:47.912 --> 02:11:50.712
People run away
with the money they embezzle.

1724
02:11:50.832 --> 02:11:55.392
With us, someone else enjoys the money.
We get to run away.

1725
02:11:55.672 --> 02:11:59.792
He's a loser.
If he goes abroad, he'll die of hunger.

1726
02:11:59.912 --> 02:12:01.472
Do you even have a passport?

1727
02:12:01.592 --> 02:12:05.392
Not a problem. Farhad's passport
still has my picture on it.

1728
02:12:06.152 --> 02:12:08.792
I just have to not get caught at the airport.

1729
02:12:24.872 --> 02:12:27.392
I wasn't gonna leave it handy.

1730
02:12:27.672 --> 02:12:29.392
I know you're upset.

1731
02:12:29.832 --> 02:12:32.192
I ruined all your documents.

1732
02:12:32.472 --> 02:12:35.992
Keep it if you want,
but I swear this is the last time.

1733
02:12:37.632 --> 02:12:39.272
Not to mention it's risky.

1734
02:12:39.392 --> 02:12:41.192
If I get caught, I could get life.

1735
02:12:41.312 --> 02:12:42.712
You're leaving for good?

1736
02:12:42.832 --> 02:12:44.992
- He can't stay.
- What can I do?

1737
02:12:45.152 --> 02:12:46.632
He has to go for good.

1738
02:12:46.752 --> 02:12:49.432
If he leaves like this,
we won't see him again.

1739
02:12:49.552 --> 02:12:52.992
- How can he leave?
- Now's not the time, Farhad.

1740
02:12:53.112 --> 02:12:55.192
What do you need your passport for?

1741
02:12:55.312 --> 02:12:56.992
I don't mean my passport.

1742
02:12:57.112 --> 02:13:00.072
I mean how can he not get caught?

1743
02:13:00.192 --> 02:13:02.192
Piss me off and I won't hand it over.

1744
02:13:27.072 --> 02:13:28.392
Here.

1745
02:13:28.952 --> 02:13:30.992
I never did anything with it.

1746
02:13:37.672 --> 02:13:39.232
Send money if you can.

1747
02:13:39.352 --> 02:13:42.392
If you can't, don't come back
and don't call too often.

1748
02:13:44.592 --> 02:13:48.592
If you do, tell us you're doing great,

1749
02:13:48.712 --> 02:13:51.192
with a good job and good money.

1750
02:13:55.832 --> 02:13:59.792
It'd be nice if we could be reassured
about you at least.

1751
02:14:31.352 --> 02:14:33.792
What if they arrest him at the airport?

1752
02:14:34.272 --> 02:14:36.592
You guys are right, I'm a coward.

1753
02:14:39.912 --> 02:14:44.392
You may not believe this,
but I'm even afraid of good things.

1754
02:14:46.312 --> 02:14:50.592
When all is well,
I wait for something bad to happen.

1755
02:14:51.832 --> 02:14:53.152
Even Maryam,

1756
02:14:53.552 --> 02:14:56.192
I couldn't keep her
because she was too good.

1757
02:14:57.152 --> 02:15:02.392
At the factory, I chose a girl
who didn't suit me from the get-go.

1758
02:15:02.512 --> 02:15:05.392
And I finally broke up with her
for those reasons.

1759
02:15:06.312 --> 02:15:10.792
I don't like imperfection,
and perfection scares me.

1760
02:15:11.072 --> 02:15:12.392
What's that mean?

1761
02:15:13.232 --> 02:15:15.392
I was afraid of the shop.

1762
02:15:16.032 --> 02:15:18.992
I'm even afraid of happiness.

1763
02:15:21.712 --> 02:15:26.192
You were taught what to think
and not how to think.

1764
02:15:39.392 --> 02:15:41.512
Give him something he likes, at least.

1765
02:15:41.632 --> 02:15:43.992
- You know him.
- No time to be picky.

1766
02:15:44.112 --> 02:15:46.592
Don't get worked up,
I'll pack it myself.

1767
02:15:47.112 --> 02:15:49.192
This is how you help him leave?

1768
02:15:50.672 --> 02:15:53.672
You're the one
who put him out on the street.

1769
02:15:53.792 --> 02:15:55.792
Who? Me?

1770
02:15:55.912 --> 02:15:57.232
Who else?

1771
02:15:57.632 --> 02:15:59.752
Isn't attack the best form of defence?

1772
02:15:59.872 --> 02:16:01.592
What're you saying, Mom?

1773
02:16:03.392 --> 02:16:04.832
She's worse than her brothers.

1774
02:16:04.952 --> 02:16:07.832
If she cared at all, she'd die of shame.

1775
02:16:07.952 --> 02:16:09.272
Don't start, Dad.

1776
02:16:09.432 --> 02:16:12.312
Don't, Leila. I'll do it.

1777
02:16:12.432 --> 02:16:16.312
- You don't know how to pack.
- Go upstairs before it degenerates.

1778
02:16:16.432 --> 02:16:20.192
What wench did your mother use
as a model to make you?

1779
02:16:20.312 --> 02:16:22.312
- She looked in the mirror.
- Shut up.

1780
02:16:22.432 --> 02:16:25.312
We'd have been better off
if you'd been sterile.

1781
02:16:25.432 --> 02:16:27.152
Why me?

1782
02:16:27.272 --> 02:16:31.352
My sons were living their lives
and earning their crust.

1783
02:16:31.472 --> 02:16:35.432
She's the one who should be sterile,
she caused their misfortune.

1784
02:16:35.552 --> 02:16:37.712
- That's enough, Mom.
- If we start finger-pointing,

1785
02:16:37.832 --> 02:16:39.592
we'll all in for it.

1786
02:16:39.712 --> 02:16:41.192
They already started.

1787
02:16:41.632 --> 02:16:43.912
If you're jobless, whose fault is it?

1788
02:16:44.032 --> 02:16:46.512
If Manouchehr is fleeing,
whose fault is it?

1789
02:16:46.632 --> 02:16:49.032
If we're humiliated,

1790
02:16:49.152 --> 02:16:51.992
if we're made fun of by friend and foe?

1791
02:16:52.112 --> 02:16:53.432
Mom...

1792
02:16:54.152 --> 02:16:56.592
Why can't the two of you just die?

1793
02:16:56.752 --> 02:17:00.152
Thank God,
it's your pain is killing every day.

1794
02:17:00.272 --> 02:17:02.192
That's enough.

1795
02:17:02.952 --> 02:17:06.232
I wouldn't be like this
if I wasn't your maid.

1796
02:17:06.352 --> 02:17:09.032
I gave birth to a lady.
You chose to become a maid.

1797
02:17:09.152 --> 02:17:12.472
You bitch, you love only yourself.

1798
02:17:12.592 --> 02:17:17.192
You hate all women.
Don't make me laugh.

1799
02:17:17.432 --> 02:17:19.512
You know why they're up shit creek?

1800
02:17:19.632 --> 02:17:22.992
Because they were raised
by you two morons.

1801
02:17:23.512 --> 02:17:27.912
You favor your husband over your sons,
and your sons over your daughter.

1802
02:17:28.032 --> 02:17:30.792
You've left your daughter
to inherit nothing but misery.

1803
02:17:30.912 --> 02:17:34.872
I had to go into debt at my age
and I'm still keeping a grip.

1804
02:17:34.992 --> 02:17:36.312
Into debt?

1805
02:17:37.112 --> 02:17:39.392
Will you ever stop lying?

1806
02:17:40.472 --> 02:17:42.992
Haven't you had your revenge?

1807
02:17:49.592 --> 02:17:51.312
Isn't this the deed to the house?

1808
02:17:52.592 --> 02:17:56.592
Didn't you make them return the shop for this?

1809
02:17:56.992 --> 02:17:58.592
Where did you leave it?

1810
02:17:58.872 --> 02:18:01.192
Why is it hidden here?

1811
02:18:01.552 --> 02:18:04.312
He's had a secret account for 20 years.

1812
02:18:04.432 --> 02:18:07.192
He bought the coins with his own money.

1813
02:18:07.432 --> 02:18:10.752
Mom, who put them out on the street?
Who, Dad?

1814
02:18:10.872 --> 02:18:15.392
Me or you, who meddled in our affairs
until we were all miserable?

1815
02:18:16.312 --> 02:18:21.152
You didn't pay for his studies.
You didn't let him marry the girl he loved.

1816
02:18:21.272 --> 02:18:24.792
- Is no one going to stop this brat?
- Brat?

1817
02:18:24.912 --> 02:18:27.992
Brats are children
who haven't had an upbringing.

1818
02:18:28.592 --> 02:18:32.152
Who haven't been encouraged
when they do good.

1819
02:18:32.272 --> 02:18:34.992
Or punished when they do wrong.

1820
02:18:35.312 --> 02:18:37.832
Punishment was reserved for children.

1821
02:18:37.952 --> 02:18:43.552
But sometimes adults need punishing
for them to stop wrecking people's lives.

1822
02:18:43.672 --> 02:18:44.992
What have you done?

1823
02:18:45.312 --> 02:18:46.992
What've you done, Leila?

1824
02:18:47.112 --> 02:18:50.912
Leila, what the hell did you just do?

1825
02:18:51.032 --> 02:18:54.792
Leila! How could you? Stay here.

1826
02:18:54.912 --> 02:18:57.472
I'm gonna kill you!

1827
02:18:57.592 --> 02:19:02.392
- Come apologize.
- Curse her!

1828
02:19:19.712 --> 02:19:23.392
Leila, may God curse you.

1829
02:20:02.792 --> 02:20:04.112
- Here you go.
- Is that it?

1830
02:20:04.232 --> 02:20:05.552
Yes, sir.

1831
02:21:34.752 --> 02:21:36.392
Your phone, sir.

1832
02:21:37.232 --> 02:21:39.592
- Why?
- They're no longer authorized.

1833
02:21:46.112 --> 02:21:48.792
The factory owes you 12 months of wages.

1834
02:21:49.592 --> 02:21:52.392
But the factory has closed.

1835
02:21:52.752 --> 02:21:54.752
Management has worked hard

1836
02:21:54.872 --> 02:21:57.392
to pay you 3 months of those wages.

1837
02:21:58.072 --> 02:22:01.472
- And the rest?
- The point is that's all you'll get.

1838
02:22:01.592 --> 02:22:04.752
I lost my benefits.
I need the full amount.

1839
02:22:04.872 --> 02:22:06.952
We can only pay 3 months.

1840
02:22:07.072 --> 02:22:12.312
And you have to sign a statement
saying our debt's been settled.

1841
02:22:12.432 --> 02:22:17.272
- You'll be paid in cash.
- You owe us a year's worth of wages,

1842
02:22:17.392 --> 02:22:20.552
and you're offering 3 months
after 90% depreciation?

1843
02:22:20.672 --> 02:22:23.952
Don't harp on.
I explained it already.

1844
02:22:24.072 --> 02:22:26.392
Whoever's interested can line up.

1845
02:22:29.912 --> 02:22:32.392
- Where you going?
- I want what I'm owed.

1846
02:22:32.632 --> 02:22:36.392
- What I worked for.
- You'll lose even this.

1847
02:22:37.192 --> 02:22:38.512
It's up to you.

1848
02:24:49.392 --> 02:24:50.792
Not on the floor.

1849
02:24:51.192 --> 02:24:53.792
Take these plates and silverware.

1850
02:24:59.912 --> 02:25:03.192
- Hello!
- Thank you.

1851
02:25:03.312 --> 02:25:05.872
You girls look lovely!
Here's my gift, sweetie.

1852
02:25:05.992 --> 02:25:08.552
- Thank you, Uncle.
- Happy birthday!

1853
02:25:08.672 --> 02:25:12.592
Look at those beautiful dresses.

1854
02:25:13.232 --> 02:25:17.992
Let's see who can blow one up fastest.

1855
02:25:18.472 --> 02:25:20.952
One... Two...

1856
02:25:21.072 --> 02:25:23.192
There's a present for the winner.

1857
02:25:23.312 --> 02:25:24.632
Three.

1858
02:25:41.032 --> 02:25:42.992
Uncle, did you lose?

1859
02:25:43.912 --> 02:25:46.792
He got scared. He's running away.

1860
02:25:47.872 --> 02:25:49.192
Dad...

1861
02:25:51.712 --> 02:25:53.032
Daddy dearest...

1862
02:25:56.112 --> 02:25:57.432
Dad...

1863
02:26:00.832 --> 02:26:02.152
Dad.

1864
02:27:27.752 --> 02:27:32.992
Come in. Welcome, my little angels.

1865
02:27:33.752 --> 02:27:35.072
Here they are!

1866
02:27:35.312 --> 02:27:37.392
Come in.

1867
02:27:37.512 --> 02:27:40.792
Come in, my lovelies.

1868
02:27:42.792 --> 02:27:45.992
Dad... Dad...

1869
02:28:17.352 --> 02:28:20.192
Uncle, come dance!

1870
02:28:20.632 --> 02:28:22.792
Come on, stand up.

1871
02:30:17.192 --> 02:30:20.192
Subtitled by: Tarjama LTD
Amman - Jordan
